{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try","id":1168631,"title":"V5 is the most-anticipated rpg of 2018 second try","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-18T14:10:24-08:00","id":1168631,"title":"V5 is the most-anticipated rpg of 2018 second try","content":"Don't know how, but seems like to me, I managed to broke the other thread's page, so there's another one for discussion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T16:12:56-08:00","id":1168661,"title":"","content":"Not really sure how they swung that... though it seems mostly like I can't think of many big releases for 2018 that aren't either already a bit spent on anticipation via crowdfunding in 2017 (ex: Numenera 2), being late (a few in the top ten were supposed to be out already), or are supplements/setting books for existing systems, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a double edged sword to be the most anticipated X of Y, because it means the bar you need to pass to become the most disappointing X of Y gets that much higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T16:24:10-08:00","id":1168665,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Martin mentioned something about the pressure on FB. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, it's quite sure that V5 will be THE rpg publication of 2018, for better or worse, it'll be either a big success and comeback to the wider audience, or a pretty spectacular flap. However, the vote was done after two rounds of palytest on three big events and then publicly, so there's that. It might, just <i>might</i> be that people are liking what they see, or at least parts of it and remained hopeful for the whole project in bigger numbers than not.<br /> <br /> Also, that it won on enWolrd, which isn't exactly a WoD fansite is still quite a feat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T17:09:10-08:00","id":1168677,"title":"","content":"Not surprised. These forums have never spoken for the majority of World of Darkness fans. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T17:31:05-08:00","id":1168682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168677#post1168677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not surprised. These forums have never spoken for the majority of World of Darkness fans.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just these forums. From time-to-time I'd happen to look up the official Shadowrun forums. Based on that, you'd think that 5e is a hot garbage, everyone's hating it, the company is ruined, all of it is on a lifeline, etc. That it's basically BAD. According to Icv2? It's the 4th biggest rpg on the market, if I remember correctly, after D&amp;D, PF, and SW... My strong suspect is that few vocal and disgruntled members just made everybody else running away.<br /> <br /> Social sites on the internet have the almost inevitable tendency of becoming echo chambers, I believe. It's not a fault of anyone, really, it's just the nature of the thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-18-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T17:36:27-08:00","id":1168684,"title":"","content":"Back on topic: I think the majority of WoD fans are just happy it'll happen and the energy coming off from WW and liked, at least partly, the playtests. Honestly, 80% of the outrage I've seen weer contained to these forums and rpg.net, with a pretty considerable overlap. People on Reddit was more evenly distributed. People on FB were mostly happy. I never heard serious complaining about their LARPS or about the playtests at the events. Everybody attended seems happy (apart from that one person at the grand Masquerade last year on the Q&amp;A and that was even before the pre-alpha).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-18-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T18:33:20-08:00","id":1168693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168682#post1168682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social sites on the internet have the almost inevitable tendency of becoming echo chambers, I believe. It's not a fault of anyone, really, it's just the nature of the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> And like you said, from here to the rpgnet forums, there is a lot of overlap. I notice a lot of the same forum users on this site and there, posting the same concerns/problems, etc. <br /> <br /> Facebook and Twitter seem to tell a different tale.<br /> <br /> Now the question is: will White Wolf be able to come through on this popularity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T18:45:12-08:00","id":1168695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168693#post1168693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Facebook and Twitter seem to tell a different tale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't follow Twitter. So, the reactions were positive over there too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now the question is: will White Wolf be able to come through on this popularity? </div> </div> </div>That's the million dollar question, I agree. Don't envy the pressure on the WW folks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So much anticipation, so much influence on so many people's lives. It's just not a thing that'll go unnoticed, another rpg in the crowd. They will either get it right and convince the existing fanbase and make it sexy for new players and all their efforts and plans with the whole brand and community stuff will be a great success story, or it will fall. Hard and in a very spectacular way. <br /> <br /> I hope it will be the first. The potential is here, the talent and knowledge, IMO is here, even if I don't personally like every part of everything they'd put out so far. It's just depending on so many things. But seeing the anticipation from the fanbase, it's heartening. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T20:19:07-08:00","id":1168709,"title":"","content":"Of course, all of this is based off of ~5,500 people voting on EN World's forum... it's not exactly any more representative of any other gaming forum.<br /> <br /> Though WW's Twitter account is pretty sparse. There's not really a lot of discussion there positive or negative.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity... where are you finding anything from ICv2 about WW besides their articles about V5 and W5 coming out eventually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T21:12:35-08:00","id":1168713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168709#post1168709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, all of this is based off of ~5,500 people voting on EN World's forum... it's not exactly any more representative of any other gaming forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet it's a <i>bit</i> more than all the membership count of this forum. 5000 people is quite standard for political polls, at least in my country. Yes, it's just a vote on an (albeit one of the biggest, if not the biggest and not even WoD-centric or even horror-oriented) rpg sites. I won't go so far to say it's representative, since I don't think there's serious methodology behind it, but it shows some things, most of all, a general anticipation from the wider fanbase.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Out of curiosity... where are you finding anything from ICv2 about WW besides their articles about V5 and W5 coming out eventually? </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's anything more about V5 on ICv2. It's not out, after all. Where did that come from? I mentioned ICv2 in relation to Shadowrun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-19-2017, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T21:48:10-08:00","id":1168717,"title":"","content":"Is any other major publisher putting out something not by KS in 2018? I mean the only thing I can think of that might even compete is the 40k and they haven't been trying to actively build the hype like NuWW. I Honestly don't see how this is even a contest. I mean even people who don't like what they've seen are anticipating seeing a fuller view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T00:33:14-08:00","id":1168732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168713#post1168713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet it's a <i>bit</i> more than all the membership count of this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... not even close. I'm sure it's more than &quot;real&quot; membership count (active users with posts, discounting bots, etc.), but the membership count on this forum is significantly higher. There isn't a page to view it, but a user's profile URL has a number that indicates their order of joining. I've seen at least one of those over 20K.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it's just a vote on an (albeit one of the biggest, if not the biggest and not even WoD-centric or even horror-oriented) rpg sites. </div> </div> </div>It is definitely big. Though it has over twice RPG.net's membership, they have about the same active user counts. I mean, we'd both agree the RPG.net forum's feelings about V5 are very different than EN World's forum, but I'm not sure how you really parse out which is a better view of the general anticipation of the wider community (though RPG.net doesn't have an equivalent poll, and EN World's threads don't seem to show nearly as much preference for V5 from the active users compared to other games on the lists, despite the vote going in a different direction from the active posters).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think there's anything more about V5 on ICv2. It's not out, after all. Where did that come from? I mentioned ICv2 in relation to Shadowrun. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, misread your post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168717#post1168717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is any other major publisher putting out something not by KS in 2018?</div> </div> </div> </div>The more they're considered 'major' the less they're likely to have something on KS, esp. the ones like WW that have financial backing from a parent company (or a profitable other product). WotC, Paizo, FFG, I don't think any of them even do KS.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:16:12-08:00","id":1168760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168717#post1168717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is any other major publisher putting out something not by KS in 2018?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless we get something like Cyberpunk 2077 (unlikely given the production speed of stuff over at R. Talsorian), 5e Planescape (even less likely) or that one upcoming book for Starfinder that has Sean Astin and Wesley Snipes as creative directors and writers (not likely that's going to be 2018) I do think that Vampire V is going to be 2018's biggest release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:40:49-08:00","id":1168777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168713#post1168713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I bet it's a <i>bit</i> more than all the membership count of this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>DEFINITELY more than the active user count of this forum. A lot more, actually. <br /> <br /> And like I said, there's a lot of overlap between these forums and the rpg.net forums. So seeing that many people vote with anticipation towards V5 is definitely a breath of fresh air compared to the small(but vocal) minority seen here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T09:59:03-08:00","id":1168831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168732#post1168732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's... not even close. I'm sure it's more than &quot;real&quot; membership count (active users with posts, discounting bots, etc.), but the membership count on this forum is significantly higher. There isn't a page to view it, but a user's profile URL has a number that indicates their order of joining. I've seen at least one of those over 20K.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, my bad, I was hasty, I thought about, as you said, real membership, aka, active (even if remotely) human users.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is definitely big. Though it has over twice RPG.net's membership, they have about the same active user counts. </div> </div> </div>It'll be interesting to see how many people are visiting the sites daily? I guess EnWorld would be bigger, just for the fact, that it's D&amp;D centric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, we'd both agree the RPG.net forum's feelings about V5 are very different than EN World's forum, </div> </div> </div>The EnWorld forum basically don't have any stance on V5, I think, because the sites main audience just isn't WoD fans (and regular users were surprised at the result, which is somewhat funny, reading posts essentially saying &quot;wow, is Vampire still a thing?&quot;). The fact that it won anyway is telling something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I'm not sure how you really parse out which is a better view of the general anticipation of the wider community (though RPG.net doesn't have an equivalent poll, and EN World's threads don't seem to show nearly as much preference for V5 from the active users compared to other games on the lists, despite the vote going in a different direction from the active posters). </div> </div> </div>What I'm seeing and why I believe it's a relevant result is this:<br /> <br /> 1. they had a poll, other sites didn't<br /> <br /> 2. the people voting for V5, I don't think are the regular users of EnWorld, since the site's focus. However, it got shared on social media, so it reached the WoD fanbase and they voted. At least that's what I think happened. That's why you won't find the reverse of rpg.net's stance regarding V5 in EnWorld's threads, because it's not really the EnWorld forum crowd's positive stance, vs. the rpg.net crowd's negative stance. I believe it's more likely the wider WoD audience's stance vs. the rpg.ne crowd's. Of course I can't prove it, but that is what I think happened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, misread your post. </div> </div> </div>Ah, no biggie!<br /> <br /> In conjunction, I must say, these forums, with all the heated arguments and disagreeing, are still a more friendly places than the Shadowrun ones. It's just tyring to read all the whining about technomancers and bashing on the company. I just wanted to point it out as an example about how forum posts aren't really good indicators, since SR5 seems to be going strong (or at least okay), despite all that. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T10:02:53-08:00","id":1168834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168717#post1168717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is any other major publisher putting out something not by KS in 2018? I mean the only thing I can think of that might even compete is the 40k and they haven't been trying to actively build the hype like NuWW. I Honestly don't see how this is even a contest. I mean even people who don't like what they've seen are anticipating seeing a fuller view.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing which is positive on itself: I can't wait the moment when I can walk in a bookstore and just buy a VtM book from the shelf, like I did during my teens-early twenties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll probably still order it through the internet, since I don't think Hungarian bookshops will carry it without a translation and an inland publisher. :/ Gaming shops might, although...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T14:38:10-08:00","id":1168920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168760#post1168760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless we get something like Cyberpunk 2077 (unlikely given the production speed of stuff over at R. Talsorian), 5e Planescape (even less likely) or that one upcoming book for Starfinder that has Sean Astin and Wesley Snipes as creative directors and writers (not likely that's going to be 2018) I do think that Vampire V is going to be 2018's biggest release.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OF those I would only count Cyberpunk as rpg vs a suppliment, perhaps Planescape. There's so little out there that being most anticipated just feels easy. I Mean even at Enworld what were they going to say instead? Pathfinder is pretty much grinding the edges so and PF2 would be pretty devisive, Starfinder is already out, 5e is already out and a 5.5 would be a temper tantrum. Every big game I can possibly think of is already out except maybe the warhammer liscence. Oh wait maybe L5R?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T14:46:07-08:00","id":1168927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168834#post1168834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing which is positive on itself: I can't wait the moment when I can walk in a bookstore and just buy a VtM book from the shelf, like I did during my teens-early twenties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll probably still order it through the internet, since I don't think Hungarian bookshops will carry it without a translation and an inland publisher. :/ Gaming shops might, although...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly unless they can do something like Adventure league being able to &quot;buy in a book store&quot; is pretty much the equivalent of being able to &quot;buy it at a gamestop&quot; now if they can get regular organized play that people can just drop into and get their vampire on. That will help everything but just being in a book store isn't really going to help much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T14:49:51-08:00","id":1168928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168920#post1168920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OF those I would only count Cyberpunk as rpg vs a suppliment, perhaps Planescape. There's so little out there that being most anticipated just feels easy. I Mean even at Enworld what were they going to say instead? Pathfinder is pretty much grinding the edges so and PF2 would be pretty devisive, Starfinder is already out, 5e is already out and a 5.5 would be a temper tantrum. Every big game I can possibly think of is already out except maybe the warhammer liscence. Oh wait maybe L5R?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Ulisses is working on a Warhammer 40k RPG now that FFG no longer has the license. So unless we're going to get a new version of GURPS or Steve Jackson Games has something else up their sleeve, 2018 will belong to Vampire V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T16:01:50-08:00","id":1168938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168927#post1168927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly unless they can do something like Adventure league being able to &quot;buy in a book store&quot; is pretty much the equivalent of being able to &quot;buy it at a gamestop&quot; now if they can get regular organized play that people can just drop into and get their vampire on. That will help everything but just being in a book store isn't really going to help much.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I'm very curious about in a good way is what exactly are they planning with WoD.com and organized play?<br /> <br /> Also, I disagree, being in a bookstore helps in my opinion. That means you have an avenue of entering for people outside the hobby. It's also good for visibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:05:12-08:00","id":1168951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1168938#post1168938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing I'm very curious about in a good way is what exactly are they planning with WoD.com and organized play?<br /> <br /> Also, I disagree, being in a bookstore helps in my opinion. That means you have an avenue of entering for people outside the hobby. It's also good for visibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using D&amp;D5 as an example of what they probably want to with v5. It has exploded out in popularity, growing the brand. I've met plenty of new people, first time gamers at Adventure league style stuff. However not one of them has ever told me &quot;I randomly picked D&amp;D up in a bookstore&quot; what they have told me is they saw people playing streams of the game online and decided to go play. That there was readily available gaming and even some training wheels for Gming.<br /> <br /> It might be very different where you are from, this might be an Europe vs America thing, but here bookstores are fading thing. Hobbystores work by being something different and perhaps that is more what you're talking about when you mean bookstores. Even then I've seen the occasional Onyx path special edition in there, maybe NuWW has the money to throw at bigger releases, but if its a choice I'd much rather see an expansion of online presence than a new shiny book that no one plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T15:38:15-08:00","id":1169501,"title":"","content":"From FB for those who don't use it:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-vie1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/25498166_10155664161930465_8170555460652931611_n.jpg?oh=ece9a61227872b683a519bcaf2b79e86&amp;oe=5AB9DAE7\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;In 2018, what stirred in the shadows will stalk the night!<br /> <br /> To celebrate Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition's placement as &quot;Most Anticipated RPG of 2018&quot; in the EN World Poll, we are sharing with you an early holiday gift: the official V5 logo! Logo design by Tomas Arfert and Chris Elliott. <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/v5\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/v5</a><br /> <br /> Our new V5 logo gives the original Vampire typeface some wear and tear to show a decaying Kindred society while a modern style for the subtitle signifies a brand new Masquerade. Overall, it reflects our return to Vampire\u2019s original vision while stepping boldly into the 21st century.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> I... Like it. Easily my favorite VtM logo this far. The ankh's incorporation is pretty cool. That it uses the 1e font and the text above is another drop in the &quot;going back to the roots&quot; basket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T20:36:05-08:00","id":1169567,"title":"","content":"Huh?<br /> <br /> Every edition used this same basic layout for the VtM title art. The font isn't 1e, since 1e's had two fonts on for &quot;Vampire,&quot; and a different one for &quot;The Masquerade.&quot; It's closer to 2e.<br /> <br /> The ankh is OK, but it's not an obvious replacement. In most fonts capital Q doesn't drop below the line of the text, or only does so a little.<br /> <br /> From a front page layout perspective, it's actually a really frustrating choice. The ankh isn't centered, but is a very intrusive (it breaks the theme and boundaries of the rest of the image) element that's aimed towards the center of a cover instead of off to the side. It draws the eye to whatever is right beneath it, which looks strange if the cover art isn't picked carefully (including potentially blank space).<br /> <br /> If it's just V5 cover ... it's not a big deal. They can tweak it to look good despite that. I figure most supplements (like every other WoD product) isn't going to slap it on the front cover prominently enough to matter if at all. Stand alone like a button in the DTRPG store isn't going to matter. Just seems... whatever. It's not a bad direction. It's simpler and at least in that contrast eye grabbing. I don't mind sacrificing the quasi-gothic fancy fonts VtM used frequently in the past. But it also doesn't do much to help with continuity of branding, showing off the fact that it's 5th Edition (like their previous V V thing), so it's pretty meh to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T21:15:27-08:00","id":1169568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169567#post1169567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh?<br /> <br /> Every edition used this same basic layout for the VtM title art. The font isn't 1e, since 1e's had two fonts on for &quot;Vampire,&quot; and a different one for &quot;The Masquerade.&quot; It's closer to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, every edition, but Revised (which was almost, but not exactly similar) used the same font for the &quot;Vampire&quot; word and used a different one for &quot;Masquerade&quot;. It's no different here. The &quot;Vampire&quot; letters are the same as 1-2 and 20th editions', although less tall, more compressed and I think for the better.<br /> <br /> I quite like the result of their attempt of mixing the old and new. I think it succeeded. Vampire seems like a chipped away tomb-script and quite gothic in that, while Masquerade is modern. It looks good, though, to be honest, I liked the &quot;fancy, quasi-gothic&quot; fonts.<br /> <br /> The ankh, I honestly didn't notice it's not in the middle, it misses it by so little. I like it replacing the Q, but it could be good under the whole text, or behind it too. If they're using the traditional rose cover (I hope so), the slight shift to the right could draw the eye to the petals. To me, it's good it doesn't shout out that it is the 5th edition, aside from V20 neither editions did so.<br /> <br /> Also, okay, it's just one-day old and I didn't look up every possible site, but you are literally the first person I seen who doesn't like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To be fair, naturally, not everyone will like it, but the responses I've seen were overwhelmingly positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-22-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T02:47:01-08:00","id":1169587,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling most of the people reacting positively to it don't have a few hundred hours of page layout under their belts, and immediately eye something like that for its intended use as a layout element over just how it looks. As well, I'm assuming they're all familiar with VtM, and have see the VtM ankh before to get where the logo is going.<br /> <br /> I saw it was off-center immediately. It's pretty much the first thing I noticed, because it's the eye catch of the piece. It's the big thing that's different, so it's the first thing your eyes want to look at. And I've spend enough hours fiddling with millimeter sized adjustments to layouts to make cool looking individual pieces look good together, that I cringe when I see things like this because I know however cool it looks in the abstract, it'll be a pain in the ass for someone to make work once they need it to look good on a cover.<br /> <br /> Stressing the new edition here is actually pretty important because it's been a very long time (at this rate it will be the second longest gap after Revised to V20) between editions, and it being new is a big part of the marketing. In a very real sense (however any of us feel about the direction) this is the first proper new edition of the game in almost twenty years. V20 is being counted as an edition, but it's Revised with a few rules tweaks and no metaplot advancement. V5 is a massive overhaul of system and setting. &quot;This is a legit brand new version of your beloved old game,&quot; is something you want to things like logos to communicate.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not going to run off to WW's social media pages to say, &quot;I think this is mediocre.&quot; I don't dislike it enough to do more than point out why here, and what I like about it not overcoming that is just my opinion. I'd imagine most people that feel like my are just as unmotivated to say anything about it (esp. in places that are more positive in general about V5, if they're even talking about it or this in particular).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T03:47:08-08:00","id":1169595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169568#post1169568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but you are literally the first person I seen who doesn't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This should not come as a surprise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The vast majority of people I've seen like it. We're talking overwhelmingly positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:16:13-08:00","id":1169742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169587#post1169587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling most of the people reacting positively to it don't have a few hundred hours of page layout under their belts, and immediately eye something like that for its intended use as a layout element over just how it looks. As well, I'm assuming they're all familiar with VtM, and have see the VtM ankh before to get where the logo is going.<br /> <br /> I saw it was off-center immediately. It's pretty much the first thing I noticed, because it's the eye catch of the piece. It's the big thing that's different, so it's the first thing your eyes want to look at. And I've spend enough hours fiddling with millimeter sized adjustments to layouts to make cool looking individual pieces look good together, that I cringe when I see things like this because I know however cool it looks in the abstract, it'll be a pain in the ass for someone to make work once they need it to look good on a cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, we're coming from very different backgrounds here. I understand your viewpoint and how you immediately notice things like that. It's the same with every field. For example, my HEMA background made it quite challenging to enjoy any fighting scenes in movies with swords (although, after a while you reach the point where you just don't care). As I said, I didn't notice it at first sight, until you brought it up and I still think the whole looks cool, it's maybe my favorite Masquerade logo (although I could imagine other alternative uses for the ankh, as I mentioned). I understand what you are saying about it being tricky to make it flawless on a cover, but I'm pretty sure they'll manage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stressing the new edition here is actually pretty important because it's been a very long time (at this rate it will be the second longest gap after Revised to V20) between editions, and it being new is a big part of the marketing. In a very real sense (however any of us feel about the direction) this is the first proper new edition of the game in almost twenty years. V20 is being counted as an edition, but it's Revised with a few rules tweaks and no metaplot advancement. V5 is a massive overhaul of system and setting. &quot;This is a legit brand new version of your beloved old game,&quot; is something you want to things like logos to communicate. </div> </div> </div>Well, some of the notable rpgs which didn't advertise the latest edition's number on the cover (or even in the Books' text, really): CoC, Shadowrun (4e and 5e), D&amp;D (4e and 5e). It seems to be the norm. I think publishers don't want to confuse new buyers with edition numbers, they want to be the new edition THE game. Naturally, we geeks are using the editions' numbers, but that is just us, for the wider world they're just D&amp;D, CoC, Shadowrun and in this case, Vampire. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T18:34:36-08:00","id":1169794,"title":"","content":"I am profoundly indifferent to the logo as it currently is. I'd like to see some cover mockups though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T20:06:28-08:00","id":1169808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169742#post1169742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, some of the notable rpgs which didn't advertise the latest edition's number on the cover (or even in the Books' text, really): CoC, Shadowrun (4e and 5e), D&amp;D (4e and 5e). It seems to be the norm. I think publishers don't want to confuse new buyers with edition numbers, they want to be the new edition THE game. Naturally, we geeks are using the editions' numbers, but that is just us, for the wider world they're just D&amp;D, CoC, Shadowrun and in this case, Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how accurate this really is, because it's not looking at things like time between editions, changes in IP ownership, and so on.<br /> Shadowrun 2e, 3e, 4e, and 20th all note that on their covers. So FASA clearly did it that way, and Catalyst did it for 4e and 20th.<br /> CoC is all over the place, because it puts out editions like mad (and more like traditional print editions where the main content is unchanged rather than how RPGs tend to use edition to mean major changes), and sometimes does, and sometimes doesn't. IIRC 6e does, but 7e doesn't (but the 20th and 25th books do too).<br /> D&amp;D is strange here, because D&amp;D doesn't have a single core book. The core sets tend to not have edition markings, but supplements frequently do. D&amp;D also makes very distinct visual choices. You can tell a 4e book from a 5e without those numbers, because the art elements are vastly different. You also have the D&amp;D Essentials between 4e and 5e that's labelled as that, and there was the attempt to get away from numerical ordering with &quot;D&amp;D Next.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it's a bit more complicated than this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T20:53:27-08:00","id":1169817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169808#post1169808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how accurate this really is, because it's not looking at things like time between editions, changes in IP ownership, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which are totally inconsequential from the average buyer's standpoint. It's not like there are tons of old edition books out there on the shelves with which you can confuse it. You'll read an article, watch a YT video, or a friend will mention Vampire, you go, you buy the book, which is new and currently available on the shelves, just like with every other game. People aren't really go looking for D&amp;D 5e, they are mostly looking for just D&amp;D and sources outside the geek community just call it D&amp;D too. So, I think stating the edition's number on the cover is out of sync with the current habits of the industry and also unnecessary. If buyers would want to learn more about the game's history, they could easily do it. Also, I'm sure it'll get mentioned int the preface, or something, that it is indeed the 5th iteration of the game. Maybe the previous V5 logo will be on the spine, I don't know, but I think it's unnecessary to incorporate it into the main title and also, it's in-line with every other edition apart from V20, which was an entirely different case, planned as the ultimate celebratory deluxe edition etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadowrun 2e, 3e, 4e, and 20th all note that on their covers. So FASA clearly did it that way, and Catalyst did it for 4e and 20th.<br /> CoC is all over the place, because it puts out editions like mad (and more like traditional print editions where the main content is unchanged rather than how RPGs tend to use edition to mean major changes), and sometimes does, and sometimes doesn't. IIRC 6e does, but 7e doesn't (but the 20th and 25th books do too).<br /> D&amp;D is strange here, because D&amp;D doesn't have a single core book. The core sets tend to not have edition markings, but supplements frequently do. D&amp;D also makes very distinct visual choices. You can tell a 4e book from a 5e without those numbers, because the art elements are vastly different. You also have the D&amp;D Essentials between 4e and 5e that's labelled as that, and there was the attempt to get away from numerical ordering with &quot;D&amp;D Next.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it's a bit more complicated than this. </div> </div> </div>Right, I looked at the SR 20th edition's cover and the text was so small, I missed it when I wrote my previous post (also, it was late).<br /> <br /> I think it was something that was customary in the past, but fallen out of habit in the past 5-10-ish years or so and got mainly reserved for anniversary editions. And again, excluding the 20ths, no major WoD core did it under any edition. Arguably, as you mentioned in the case of D&amp;D, this logo already does the job of differentiating it from previous editions in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T02:01:15-08:00","id":1169855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169817#post1169817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which are totally inconsequential from the average buyer's standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of resources companies put into these sorts of consideration would indicate otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not like there are tons of old edition books out there on the shelves with which you can confuse it. </div> </div> </div>See, it's actually worse now, because so much shopping is done online (even with lots of RPG publishers desperate to get back into physical stores). People looking for good deals on Amazon or eBay frequently end up asking people that they know are fans (even going to forums about it) to figure out which edition something is because sellers aren't always clear (or might not even know themselves). Just going to the store and buying the most currently available thing isn't even an option for at least 95% of RPGs, and at least around here, a lot of stores that stock RPG books have a clutter of old edition books mixed in with anything that isn't the latest D&amp;D, FFG, or Paizo books. Some even prominently display older books because they're trying to sell them to collectors (esp. in non-gaming primary shops, like comic book stores that also stock gaming stuff).<br /> <br /> The CofD has been the official thing for the old nWoD brand for two years now, and I still see people confused by it despite it being really easy to find information on (like the first thing I get when I Google &quot;chronicles of darkness&quot; is the fan wikia which actually explains how the CofD is a different set of games from the cWoD, and the naming thing).<br /> <br /> So yeah, this stuff does actually matter to consumers, even if it isn't always a direct or conscious thing.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D is a relatively unique position in this stuff because it is still &quot;the RPG&quot; to most people. It's an outlier that really doesn't say how everyone else needs to operate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I think stating the edition's number on the cover is out of sync with the current habits of the industry and also unnecessary. </div> </div> </div>I really don't see the evidence for this. Getting past the limited selection of books you picked out (which are the ones with the most physical store presence because they're tied to companies that do physical distribution by necessity for things like CCGs, minis, etc.), you see extremely little consensus, because it really seems far more situational and company based than you want to accept. The more games you look at, the less there seems to be any direct consistency around this like you seem to be claiming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If buyers would want to learn more about the game's history, they could easily do it. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But a huge part of the reason to buy V5 is that it is a game with history. That's a giant part of the marketing here. That's why WW funded a documentary about VtM. They want people to know that this isn't some brand new thing trying to push into the crowded RPG world. It's an old thing with a new energy coming back for it's place near the top. Customers need to see that on the cover in a simple and direct way to connect the new book to the marketing..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T06:39:38-08:00","id":1169906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169817#post1169817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I think stating the edition's number on the cover is out of sync with the current habits of the industry and also unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is 100% correct. Across all forms of entertainment media, we are seeing the same thing.<br /> <br /> Old IP's are coming back, and they're doing a &quot;back to basics&quot; approach, in a way the a new customer won't feel left out.<br /> <br /> You are seeing this being especially the case in the video game industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T14:34:47-08:00","id":1170280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1169794#post1169794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am profoundly indifferent to the logo as it currently is. I'd like to see some cover mockups though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is hopefully better then V20's cover art: hard to get any worse then that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T19:54:46-08:00","id":1170345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1170280#post1170280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is hopefully better then V20's cover art: hard to get any worse then that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V20's cover is any different than Revised or 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T21:11:31-08:00","id":1170362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1170345#post1170345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20's cover is any different than Revised or 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, considering it doesn't even have the familiar red rose.<br /> <br /> No, a carving of roses on the ankh doesn't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T10:46:25-08:00","id":1170479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1170362#post1170362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yeah, considering it doesn't even have the familiar red rose.<br /> <br /> No, a carving of roses on the ankh doesn't count.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see a red rose in this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T10:54:37-08:00","id":1170482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1170362#post1170362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, considering it doesn't even have the familiar red rose.<br /> <br /> No, a carving of roses on the ankh doesn't count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Revenant has a rose on the cover, V20 does not. Ergo, Revenant is the better game.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/f/f7/RevenantTheRavishingCover.png/revision/latest?cb=20090619211236\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T12:57:20-08:00","id":1170510,"title":"","content":"Aren't we talking about the v5 logo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T06:24:22-08:00","id":1177571,"title":"","content":"People are possitive? What happened with the second playtest, I must've missed that. <br /> <br /> After the first, with the god awful -every discipline uses blood and is built for larp not tabletop- and the sites with -incredibly shity larp pictures- and the absolute abomination of werewolf (shit tribal weaknesses, garou have dayjobs, Black furies take men, Good crafted fetishes are the fianna speciality) I had absolutely zero hope for anything there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T07:18:13-08:00","id":1177581,"title":"","content":"It is really hard to say at this point. Nearly every thing I have heard has been overwelmingly negative, and unhopeful about V5, with two exceptions. Non-WoD fans and primarily LARP fans seem to be rather impressed, as are folks that prefer rules-lite or no rules systems.<br /> <br /> Outside of those, , most people are mot happy with so many different things, and it is not usually just one or two. However, and this is that grain of salt part, most of us tend to visit sites, talk to people, or whatever that think similarly to ourselves when it comes to things like this. Or post in forums that generally align closer to our own political/social/religious leanings, which can play a large part in the opinions we hear.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it is really not that hard to twist/cook numbers for things like polls, or prioritize &quot;positive&quot; reviews and the like.<br /> <br /> I personally have not seen or heard anything suggesting people are excited, happy, or really looking foreward to V5 (other than to get to 6th Ed), but I don't frequent a lot of places where that might be a thing. Maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T07:34:26-08:00","id":1177585,"title":"","content":"From my point of view, the absolute lack of anything particularly meaningful from White Wolf, (we get an image, and a pretty uninspiring one at that as the biggest news and two rather uninspiring/incomplete playtests that show just about nothing pertinent), does not speak well for all of these so called big plans.<br /> <br /> It actually kind of reminds me of how 4th Ed D&amp;D tried to garner love. Trash talked prior editions, made all sorts of promises about both returning the game to its roots and finding ways to fix past issues, and would be the end all, be all of gaming. They had similar polls as well, as I recall, and would occassionally drop articles that ultimately didn't really say anything or the occasional art piece, but when it actually came out it was, to a lot of people at least, ... not great.<br /> <br /> It probably split the fan base moreso than anything else combined, turned people away from the brand completely, and nearly every promise made about fixing rules or systems did so by either not including that system at all, or simply making it a pointless choice. Granted, there are some fans of 4E, and that is fine. But, now that it has finally gotten past that edition, they have, at least partially officially admitted it was not all that they had hoped for across the board.<br /> <br /> I truely hope V5 is not like that. I do. But I can not help but remember that 4E era, and am not at all confident that V5 is not simply going to be a worse blunder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T14:55:59-08:00","id":1177692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177571#post1177571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened with the second playtest, I must've missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second playtest wasn't great, but it was a huge improvement over the first. The mechanics haven't fixed a lot of the core issues I have with their design decisions, but they're starting to refine things at least. The actual scenario attached was a massive step up...though who they hired to write it is probably a part of that.<br /> <br /> The second one certainly didn't sell me on V5 at all, but even I have to admit they're at least starting to realize that the first one demonstrated a severe lack of quality.<br /> <br /> Of course both previews are bad because WW doesn't seem to get why the alpha/beta test divide is supposed to entail. Alpha playtests are <b>not supposed to be public</b>. Alpha is when you're still hammering out everything and lots of stuff changes. You don't put them out to the public because they rarely represent anything close to the final product, and playtesting is done with preselected small groups; though this is harder to pull off in today's world since leaks are pretty much a given too.<br /> <br /> Beta is when you start doing big public playtests, because beta means you're at the point where the majority of the game is already designed and you want extra eyes to refine everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After the first, with the god awful -every discipline uses blood and is built for larp not tabletop- and the sites with -incredibly shity larp pictures- and the absolute abomination of werewolf (shit tribal weaknesses, garou have dayjobs, Black furies take men, Good crafted fetishes are the fianna speciality) I had absolutely zero hope for anything there. </div> </div> </div>The website in question is very poorly being marketed. WW is testing their community support portal for their LARPers first, so all the information on there is from the BNS MET books, rather than either the 20th TT books, or even their own 5th books. However to know this you have to haven been listening to certain WW people online or at cons talk about what they're doing, rather than it actually being explained there.<br /> <br /> That's why it's all LARP picture, and all the Tribal stuff is from the BNS MET WtA book. While I don't think it's promising to take too much from that book for W5, it's not clear how much BNS is bleeding into WW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177581#post1177581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-WoD fans and primarily LARP fans seem to be rather impressed, as are folks that prefer rules-lite or no rules systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really can't be too much of a surprise. WW's current team comes heavily from the LARP side of the WoD community. It's where they have the most connections, and have been doing the most outreach.<br /> <br /> While I have no issue with WW doing community outreach to more groups, we've seen pretty much zero aimed at the TT fans of their properties. They have people who's job is community support,,, that haven't even bothered making an account here to make themselves known to the fans of the people current doing all the hard work for their IPs.. and have like, four posts in on some other forums. If it's not LARP focused, they're ignoring it... which seems strange if they want to promote a new TT edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, it is really not that hard to twist/cook numbers for things like polls, or prioritize &quot;positive&quot; reviews and the like. </div> </div> </div>It's also a pretty meaningless poll. There are &quot;winners&quot; on that poll that have won multiple years in a row. I doubt WW gave two shits about that poll while it was being run to do anything like push the numbers; especially since V5 getting out in '18 seems pretty unlikely. January is almost over, and we haven't heard about V5 getting to a beta phase let alone finalization of the text. Then there's editing, rewrites, proofing, art and layout, printing, print proofs, distribution... all that shit takes months and months to get done. The people they have hired for that side of things do get it done, but their past products were not know for moving through those finalization and distribution phases quickly. <br /> <br /> I would not want an RPG I was working on, on that poll until I was way closer to publication than WW was with V5 when the poll was conducted; even WW is smart enough to not cook a poll that could easily bite them in the ass because getting out in '18 isn't nearly set in stone yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177585#post1177585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually kind of reminds me of how 4th Ed D&amp;D tried to garner love. Trash talked prior editions, made all sorts of promises about both returning the game to its roots and finding ways to fix past issues, and would be the end all, be all of gaming. They had similar polls as well, as I recall, and would occassionally drop articles that ultimately didn't really say anything or the occasional art piece, but when it actually came out it was, to a lot of people at least, ... not great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what's most problematic for the chance to repeat D&amp;D 4e's issues is that the WoD fan-community is already pretty fractured. The TT vs. LARP divide is ancient, and the WoD vs. CofD divide is still a thing (something WW is actually making worse as the CofD were moving well into being their own thing, and now V5 is using CofD design concepts). The D&amp;D community before 4e wasn't exactly unified, but beyond the normal edition wars, there wasn't as much in the ways of big cracks you could already see; and it pushed on tiny cracks that turned out to be major fissure points. WW and V5 are pushing on already visible community fractures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T17:03:40-08:00","id":1177720,"title":"","content":"It's a downright abomination. I really don't like some of the 20th stuff, some of DAV and Mage has been absolutely agonizing to read, the quality and direction of writing has been really very inconsistent with all the freelancers, but what I've read of v5, well they've just shown that they're going to consistently create a travestry and have no knowledge of what they're working with. <b>You do not shackle the power of imagination with the limitations of larp</b>. Garou do not commonly have<i> dayjobs</i>, do they not understand rage? Vampires don't spend blood for dominate, that's some basic metaphysics. Fianna fetishes aren't known for their craftsmanship, but their tales, that's the most defining trait of the fianna, alcoholism and metis bashing aside (craftsmanship; Get, Maybe SF and GW). The furies accepting male garou with working seed... well, obviously they just don't get the fucking <i>point </i>. If you're going to stifle creativity so that the game variant where you run around dressed up seems like the default, then you're making a bad game. <br /> <br /> <i>PS larpers make terrible photos. The best pictures were borderline acceptable. If you need live action, don't use someone posing for fun. Grab a professional model, use a full pro team for the shoot, edit heavily. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T22:58:39-08:00","id":1177781,"title":"","content":"Nothing about the playtests dropped shouted &quot;THIS IS REALLY LARPABLE&quot; honestly it came off as extremely finicky and slowing down alot of the advantages of Larp vs table top. I understand there's a strong &quot;blame the heretic&quot; vibe but the choices seem to be purely independently developed.<br /> <br /> Also I'll repeat again there's next to nothing else coming out in 2018 so being the most hyped game in 2018 isn't exactly hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T02:39:02-08:00","id":1177807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177720#post1177720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't spend blood for dominate, that's some basic metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? This... seems an odd complaint. There isn't some strict metaphysical basis for when Disciplines cost blood or even willpower. The assignments of costs have always seemed to be more on the game side of things to keep things from getting spammed by attaching a limited resource to it. The VtM: Bloodlines video game frequently had you spend blood on things that you don't in the TT rules, because the assumptions of the mechanics are different.<br /> <br /> V5's Hunger mechanics (something I very much dislike) also isn't the same as spending blood in a key way: you can in theory do it as much as you want. From the context of &quot;all Disciplines are an expression of the power of the Beast,&quot; and, &quot;any time a vampire calls on the power of the Beast, they risk growing hungry and must feed to sate it or risk losing control,&quot; having every Discipline invoke Hunger makes sense. The rules are still bad IMO, but within the framework WW wants to use, this does make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fianna fetishes aren't known for their craftsmanship, but their tales, that's the most defining trait of the fianna, alcoholism and metis bashing aside (craftsmanship; Get, Maybe SF and GW). </div> </div> </div>Eh? Again, not really about the One WoD or W5, but about the BNS WtA book. The Fianna are not prominently known in the rest of the Nation as such, but have been consistently portrayed as caring deeply about it internally. The flat out best talen/fetish maker Totem in the books is Brigid... who shows up in Fianna Revised (and you also have a few other Fianna associated Totems that can be good for this sort of thing). The Fianna are generally portrayed as one of the most artistic oriented Tribes. It's also a Merit, not a default bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The furies accepting male garou with working seed... well, obviously they just don't get the fucking <i>point </i>. </div> </div> </div>Other threads have debated this, and I'm not going to get into it here, but the idea of the Furies growing more inclusive to honor their commitment to help all oppressed peoples as feminism has changed a lot in the past 25 years and more of the Tribe are going to have grown up with third-wave and post-third-wave feminist values isn't necessarily &quot;missing the point,&quot; as much as, &quot;adapting the average Fury PC feminism to better reflect the current generation.&quot; Based on just the differences between BNS WtA and what WW forced into W20: Changing Ways... I'm definitely thinking that if W5 follows BNS's suit, it will be utter garbage. But that doesn't mean the initial idea lacks any merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>PS larpers make terrible photos. The best pictures were borderline acceptable. If you need live action, don't use someone posing for fun. Grab a professional model, use a full pro team for the shoot, edit heavily. </i> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this is good advice for a LARP focused website. It's certainly good advice for a general TT book - though professional model is overrated (we're talking getting a single still, not a full photo shoot), plenty of V20's photo models aren't and have good pics - but in a LARP book, the wisdom seems to be more that LARPers want to see people LARPing instead. And, again, the photos you're talking about are from the BNS LARP art stuff.<br /> <br /> It seems logical to me. In a LARP book or a LARP website, you want to show what people will actually look like, not what you can do with a professional photo team, and professional digital photo editors.<br /> <br /> IIRC - it's been awhile - the V5 pre-alpha was practical artless, and the alpha was minimal and reused stuff (they are playtest documents anyway, art's not a big concern for them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T16:16:29-08:00","id":1177961,"title":"","content":"I'm cautiously optimistic for V5. On the one hand, I detest NuWW's decision to resume the metaplot from Revised and we all know my opinions on Martin Ericsson, but with Mark Rein-Hagen as a consultant for V5 and a promise to go back to the roots of 1e (my favorite edition), I will purchase V5 when it is released and see how it goes. To me, V5 is either going to be really awesome or really horrible and it's a 50/50 shot either way.<br /> <br /> I'm one of the few people here to criticize NuWW for their actual gaming decisions (such as continuing the metaplot and certain mechanical changes in the playtests) and not merely oppose them for political reasons. And for the sake of civility, let's just leave it at that and not drag politics into this thread, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T17:45:25-08:00","id":1177971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177961#post1177961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..but with Mark Rein-Hagen as a consultant for V5 and a promise to go back to the roots of 1e (my favorite edition),...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bringing in Mark Rein-Hagen is very much a bad move for me. Even if I didn't have strong opinions about him as a human being, he's a Steve Jobs, not a Steven Wozniak; which they're already have in Martin anyway.<br /> <br /> Mark's skill in RPG's is more turning what the game designers built into a brand, than actually creating a good game in the first place. Hiring him says to me that WW is becoming the next NeXT, not what Apple became after buying NeXT out after it failed (aka the Apple of today). WW needs a solid team under people like Martin and Mark, not more people with brand vision, to actually make a good game, and we can only hope that Tobias and Jason keep there from being a repeat of Lion Rampart needing bailing out by White Wolf Magazine, and then Mark getting kicked out of the original WW for repeated the same financial mistakes that tanked Lion Rampart.<br /> <br /> I'm using the Apple comparison explicitly because of WW's stated desires towards brand recognition and expansion. They want to build up the WoD as a brand to engage in a transmedia strategy, not just to be a strong horror RPG publisher. The only problem with the analogy to me is that I have no idea who would buy WW out if V5 tanks and Paradox is thinking of off-loading it before it becomes a money drain; since there isn't the Apple/NeXT dynamic.<br /> <br /> I mean, he's a consultant, right? What's the last big creative idea he's had since 1991? What's he consulting on that's a solid reason to anticipate V5 more?<br /> <br /> I also don't see much of a promise to &quot;go back to the roots of 1e.&quot; There's some of it, I guess, in refocusing on the conflict between the Anarchs and the Camarilla, but I haven't seen anything else that really screams 1e aesthetics, and a bunch of decidedly not 1e things (like humans having vampire detecting metal detectors, and trained anti-vampire special forces) that don't seem to be a return to roots at all. The new Hunger and Humanity mechanics most certainly aren't a return to roots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm one of the few people here to criticize NuWW for their actual gaming decisions (such as continuing the metaplot and certain mechanical changes in the playtests) and not merely oppose them for political reasons. </div> </div> </div>Some of us criticize them for both quite successfully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for the sake of civility, let's just leave it at that and not drag politics into this thread, please? </div> </div> </div>For the sake of civility lets (1) not pretend that politics isn't part of this discussion, since all art and entertainment are political statements, and (2) recognize that asking people to &quot;not drag politics&quot; into a thread is a political act of trying to keep politics you don't want discussed from being discussed.<br /> <br /> Politics are absolutely one of the reasons V5 is being anticipated by people, because VtM has always been an unabashedly political game (in the sense of directly addressing real life political topics, not just having in-game political bickering). A lot of the negative reactions to V5 are because people are worried about a negative direction in those political statements by the game, instead of a positive move in addressing politics in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-21-2018, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T19:01:48-08:00","id":1177982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177961#post1177961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm cautiously optimistic for V5. On the one hand, I detest NuWW's decision to resume the metaplot from Revised and we all know my opinions on Martin Ericsson, but with Mark Rein-Hagen as a consultant for V5 and a promise to go back to the roots of 1e (my favorite edition), I will purchase V5 when it is released and see how it goes. To me, V5 is either going to be really awesome or really horrible and it's a 50/50 shot either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the names on the developer and consultant team list are pretty impressive. I just don't see how they could give something out of their hand in the end, which is a dumpster fire. I don't think they'd give their names to that. You don't want to be the person, who fucked up the new edition of Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, V5 is either going to be really awesome or really horrible and it's a 50/50 shot either way. </div> </div> </div>Agree, although I suspect we wouldn't like the same things, but still, agree. It will be awesome, or D&amp;D 4e, but it has the potential to be awesome and the anticipation is there, from the fanbase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for the sake of civility, let's just leave it at that and not drag politics into this thread, please? </div> </div> </div>sigh... At this point WW Wouldn't be able to order a coffee machine without being burned at the stake by some people. I just acknowledged it and moved on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-21-2018, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T05:10:05-08:00","id":1178039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1177971#post1177971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> For the sake of civility lets (1) not pretend that politics isn't part of this discussion, since all art and entertainment are political statements, and (2) recognize that asking people to &quot;not drag politics&quot; into a thread is a political act of trying to keep politics you don't want discussed from being discussed.<br /> <br /> Politics are absolutely one of the reasons V5 is being anticipated by people, because VtM has always been an unabashedly political game (in the sense of directly addressing real life political topics, not just having in-game political bickering). A lot of the negative reactions to V5 are because people are worried about a negative direction in those political statements by the game, instead of a positive move in addressing politics in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this whole &quot;everything is political&quot; bullshit is one of the problems with our culture today. Not all art or entertainment has to be political. I'm sick of the censorship (and yes, it is censorship even if it's not from the government). Do keep in mind that this is not meant as a personal attack on you or your personal political beliefs, but instead a criticism of your specific statement of &quot;all art and entertainment must be political&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's be frank here, World of Darkness is just a series of pretend monster games that people play for fun. Nothing more and nothing less. Attempting to drag &quot;deep&quot; political meaning into these games is just asking for trouble on all fronts from all sides of the political spectrum. Especially for people who like me who hate politics as a general rule and just want to have fun.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why I post more often at RPG Pub (an explicitly apolitical forum) these days than I do here. I'm tired of all the political debates and controversies. I just want to play my pretend monster games, that's all. It's bad enough that people here give me shit for not playing personal horror. Do we really need to drag real-life politics into this debate?<br /> <br /> Now, you are entitled to your opinion and I respect that, but let's not make something out of nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T05:26:15-08:00","id":1178040,"title":"","content":"No, WoD has always been a satirical take on the real world (some shit's so bad it must've been the work of evil monsters) You just don't do it without politics. Hell, any good game of vampire is only about politics. Midnight siege? Best book ever about cammy and sabbat confrontations... and it's really political. Werewolf, that's your satire of reactionaries and would be revolutionaries. Every line presents a dichotomy of political factions for your very scrutiny. I really don't want to post about politics here, but denying that WoD has a political persuasion is like saying there's no salt in the sea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T05:50:22-08:00","id":1178048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178040#post1178040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, WoD has always been a satirical take on the real world (some shit's so bad it must've been the work of evil monsters) You just don't do it without politics. Hell, any good game of vampire is only about politics. Midnight siege? Best book ever about cammy and sabbat confrontations... and it's really political. Werewolf, that's your satire of reactionaries and would be revolutionaries. Every line presents a dichotomy of political factions for your very scrutiny. I really don't want to post about politics here, but denying that WoD has a political persuasion is like saying there's no salt in the sea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but the politics of WoD are fictional politics between fictional in-game factions, not real life political issues, and the games were written in the 1990's. WoD is not supposed to be reflective of the fucked-up and ultra-polarized real-life political battlefields of the 2010's. Especially not in a realistic or &quot;deep&quot; sort of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:35:03-08:00","id":1178084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178048#post1178048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but the politics of WoD are fictional politics between fictional in-game factions, not real life political issues, and the games were written in the 1990's. WoD is not supposed to be reflective of the fucked-up and ultra-polarized real-life political battlefields of the 2010's. Especially not in a realistic or &quot;deep&quot; sort of way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you Read W20? It's all raw and as close to the reader as it can manage to make sure that the Rage hits home. The new Pentex subsidiary of the RED Network is extremely timely, and everything about Endron never stopped being timely even after Enron folded, because greed permeates the petroleum industry like its product..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:22:09-08:00","id":1178095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178084#post1178084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you Read W20? It's all raw and as close to the reader as it can manage to make sure that the Rage hits home. The new Pentex subsidiary of the RED Network is extremely timely, and everything about Endron never stopped being timely even after Enron folded, because greed permeates the petroleum industry like its product..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With the exception of the V20 and W20 corebooks, I quit following Classic WoD when Revised happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:29:11-08:00","id":1178097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178039#post1178039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, this whole &quot;everything is political&quot; bullshit is one of the problems with our culture today. Not all art or entertainment has to be political. I'm sick of the censorship (and yes, it is censorship even if it's not from the government). Do keep in mind that this is not meant as a personal attack on you or your personal political beliefs, but instead a criticism of your specific statement of &quot;all art and entertainment must be political&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All human discourse is political. There is no such thing as &quot;White Room&quot; discussion. Each and everything we say and write is based upon our opinions and life experiences. So unless you have an White Room AI writing Entertainment this is a bullshit statement. I could go on but this is probably the best explanation of the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be frank here, World of Darkness is just a series of pretend monster games that people play for fun. Nothing more and nothing less. Attempting to drag &quot;deep&quot; political meaning into these games is just asking for trouble on all fronts from all sides of the political spectrum. Especially for people who like me who hate politics as a general rule and just want to have fun. </div> </div> </div>Its a series of pretend monster games that say something political.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eat the Rich&quot;-Vampire.<br /> <br /> &quot;The world is dying why aren't you angry!&quot;-Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Mage is Litterally about battles of ideology.<br /> <br /> Wraith includes &quot;THE MAN&quot; litterally enslaving the majority of people and making quite afew of them into BRICKS.<br /> <br /> Changeling is about how society is destroying your dreams.<br /> <br /> Hunter, No you can't just close your eyes to this shit and say &quot;I WANT POLITICS TO GO AWAY&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't D&amp;D(Which I would still argue has political overtones BUT that they can be more easily covered up) this is something that has from its very beginnings been about engaging with politics, either its about being a transgressive outsider fighting against the Man. Or Being the Man and trying to keep things in their place.<br /> <br /> There's reason WW has since its very foundation called itself &quot;GOTH PUNK&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a reason why I post more often at RPG Pub (an explicitly apolitical forum) these days than I do here. I'm tired of all the political debates and controversies. I just want to play my pretend monster games, that's all. It's bad enough that people here give me shit for not playing personal horror. Do we really need to drag real-life politics into this debate? </div> </div> </div>Claiming Apolitcalness is just blinding yourself to your biases.<br /> <br /> The apolitical pretend to be a vampire game is... you wake up. You feed on rats. And do not engage in anything at all because... that's politicing and possibly has real world symbolism because.. its based on the real world. I mean I GUESS you could be playing Vampire:The Forgotten Realms or something though!<br /> <br /> <br /> You are not above, outside, or Apolitical when you play a pure wish fullfilment, Trenchcoat and Katanas game. Every Tribe, every Clan, Every Sect, Every Tradition, Every Convention has something to say just by picking it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:37:21-08:00","id":1178100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178095#post1178095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> With the exception of the V20 and W20 corebooks, I quit following Classic WoD when Revised happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you did read it, then?<br /> <br /> (Also, you missed Werewolf ramping up. Its metaplot was barely noticeable, if present at all, and the books existed to give groups more hooks and details to use. There was no definite date for the Apocalypse, and you could make whatever it you wanted, whenever, or just not use it and pick out some mechanical bits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:25:36-08:00","id":1178120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178097#post1178097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> All human discourse is political. There is no such thing as &quot;White Room&quot; discussion. Each and everything we say and write is based upon our opinions and life experiences. So unless you have an White Room AI writing Entertainment this is a bullshit statement. I could go on but this is probably the best explanation of the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryz_lA3Dn4c&amp;vl=en </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Its a series of pretend monster games that say something political.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eat the Rich&quot;-Vampire.<br /> <br /> &quot;The world is dying why aren't you angry!&quot;-Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Mage is Litterally about battles of ideology.<br /> <br /> Wraith includes &quot;THE MAN&quot; litterally enslaving the majority of people and making quite afew of them into BRICKS.<br /> <br /> Changeling is about how society is destroying your dreams.<br /> <br /> Hunter, No you can't just close your eyes to this shit and say &quot;I WANT POLITICS TO GO AWAY&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't D&amp;D(Which I would still argue has political overtones BUT that they can be more easily covered up) this is something that has from its very beginnings been about engaging with politics, either its about being a transgressive outsider fighting against the Man. Or Being the Man and trying to keep things in their place.<br /> <br /> There's reason WW has since its very foundation called itself &quot;GOTH PUNK&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Claiming Apolitcalness is just blinding yourself to your biases.<br /> <br /> The apolitical pretend to be a vampire game is... you wake up. You feed on rats. And do not engage in anything at all because... that's politicing and possibly has real world symbolism because.. its based on the real world. I mean I GUESS you could be playing Vampire:The Forgotten Realms or something though!<br /> <br /> <br /> You are not above, outside, or Apolitical when you play a pure wish fullfilment, Trenchcoat and Katanas game. Every Tribe, every Clan, Every Sect, Every Tradition, Every Convention has something to say just by picking it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't do Gothic-Punk, though there is nothing wrong with doing so. And you say Trenchcoats and Katanas like it's a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Let's just agree to disagree, shall we? I'm not going to sully myself by arguing over real-life political implications in pretend monster games.<br /> <br /> I don't do the metaplot and I don't do personal horror. I've established this multiple times on this forum since joining back in 2013.<br /> <br /> If you want to turn your campaigns into a political debate team, more power to you. I just want to have fun. The point of gaming is a temporary escape from the burdens of real life. I'm all down for fictional politics in the World of Darkness, but I'll be damned if I drag real-life controversies and political agendas into the gaming table because that's just asking for trouble outside of the game.<br /> <br /> If you must know my political views. I lean left, but not far left. I'm fiscally liberal and socially libertarian. I believe in a strong welfare state founded on mixed market socialism and a democratic republic. I support free speech, free expression, freedom of religion, LGBT rights, and individual liberty. I vehemently oppose extremist and totalitarian ideologies such as Fascism, Nazism, Communism, Theocracy, and Anarchism (the first three ideologies are the tyranny of the state, the other is tyranny of the church, while the last one is the tyranny of mob rule). I am a registered member of the Democratic Party in the Commonwealth of Virginia, and I supported Bernie Sanders in the primaries and voted for Jill Stein in the 2016 election, as I did not want to cast my vote for either Hillary Clinton or Orange Berlusconi.<br /> <br /> So, there. That's my political viewpoint. But I do my best to keep my political life and my gaming life separate.<br /> <br /> Can we please get this discussion back on track? Let's talk about V5, whether it's in support of it or against it, and leave the political debates for the Off-Topic sub-forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 01-22-2018, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:44:38-08:00","id":1178126,"title":"","content":"As a requiem player i am looking at V5 with mild curiosity. There is the hunger mechanic that caught my eye. If it is any fun i will probably look at incorporating it in requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:00:19-08:00","id":1178219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178039#post1178039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this whole &quot;everything is political&quot; bullshit is one of the problems with our culture today. Not all art or entertainment has to be political.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking this is something new is problematic for any discussion of it. Hell, one of the most famous articulations of this concept was by the guy that died over 67 years ago (that would be George Orwell).<br /> <br /> It is a strange and relatively constant thing that artists and entertainers are usually the ones most strongly pushing for the idea that art and entertainment are inherently political, while it's consumers that seem to make up the majority of people that want to claim it isn't. If the people that make your art say it's political (and boy howdy the people that have made the WoD over the years are all of that stance)... it's kinda hard to justify arguing with them on at least the game we're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sick of the censorship (and yes, it is censorship even if it's not from the government). </div> </div> </div>Calling something political isn't censoring it. It's ensuring that it's seen in it's full context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be frank here, World of Darkness is just a series of pretend monster games that people play for fun. Nothing more and nothing less. </div> </div> </div>And this is why I asked you to recognize what you're doing is actually making a political statement. By claiming there are no &quot;real&quot; politics in the WoD games, that they're just fun and nothing else, you are attempting to erase (censor even!) the explicit political concepts the game creators included to be explored. You're saying those politics don't count as &quot;real&quot; politics simply because you don't engage with that side of the game.<br /> <br /> You don't have to engage with the politics of the game. But when you call on others not to do so, you're making a political statement. You can say you hate politics all you want, but all it comes off as doing, is shutting down discussions of things that might need to be discussed for your own personal emotional benefit.<br /> <br /> I'll also note that you single-handedly turned this thread into an overt political discussion. I <i>mentioned</i> that there's merit to the concept of the changes in real world feminism being reflected in changes to the Black Furies - a Tribe deeply connected to feminist ideals - even if the execution sucks, but that there's other threads on it and it shouldn't be gone into thoroughly here. That's the only overt political statement I can find in the whole thread. Then you came in complaining about politics in games and we're talking about that for a whole page or more now.<br /> <br /> All over something there was no hint of growing beyond a snippet in a post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just want to play my pretend monster games, that's all. It's bad enough that people here give me shit for not playing personal horror. Do we really need to drag real-life politics into this debate? </div> </div> </div>To the middle first: if people are actually attacking you over your playstyle, report them. It's an infraction worth offense. You might need to be insistent about it, but it's not good behavior. It is worth thinking about where you post what though. The CofD and WoD are explicitly horror genre games, even if you don't play them that way, as they're explicitly political games, even if you don't engage with that aspect of them personally. It's pretty easy to get into snipes with people that feel you're attacking the games as written that they enjoy more than expressing what's fun for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178120#post1178120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you say Trenchcoats and Katanas like it's a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the point is that playing WoD as Trenchcoats and Katanas while claiming there's no political statement behind that choice, is actually a political statement in it's own right.<br /> <br /> Nobody forced you to jump into this thread, challenged you on the vast majority of your beliefs/etc, or anything. You're posting all this under your own volition , and steering things into areas you say you wish we'd stop talking about...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to sully myself by arguing over real-life political implications in pretend monster games. </div> </div> </div>And it's stuff like this that doesn't help. You're saying that discussing the political <b>messages</b> explicitly put into our pretend monster games is somehow an experience that inherently lessens people.<br /> <br /> If people read 1984, or Animal Farm, and then have a discussion about Orwell's political messages... are then sullying themselves? Are they reducing the artistic value of those stories? Or are they engaging with exactly what the artist wanted them to be engaging with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of gaming is a temporary escape from the burdens of real life. </div> </div> </div>Seen, this is what we mean by trying to be apolitical just means being political without recognizing it for what it is.<br /> <br /> Humans have been playing games since as long as there's been humans. We have never just done it for one reason. Escapism is certainly one reason. Education is another reason. Skills training is another reason. Etc. Games are vehicles for safely exploring topics, including politics.<br /> <br /> When you say, &quot;I play games to escape from X in the real world,&quot; you're making an inherently political statement about X.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm all down for fictional politics in the World of Darkness, but I'll be damned if I drag real-life controversies and political agendas into the gaming table because that's just asking for trouble outside of the game. </div> </div> </div>So, to beat the dead horse:<br /> <br /> Who asked you to?<br /> <br /> Why is it OK for you to judge what is and isn't OK for other people to talk about in regards to our pretend monster games here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can we please get this discussion back on track? </div> </div> </div>If you want it back on track... post something about V5 already.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178126#post1178126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a requiem player i am looking at V5 with mild curiosity. There is the hunger mechanic that caught my eye. If it is any fun i will probably look at incorporating it in requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take Beast's Satiety system and graft it onto Blood Potency for tracking blood expenditures (or even let it replace Humanity if you want to go that route). It's better in pretty much every way, already built for the CofD, and is actually good at giving players a reason to play hungry predators instead of doing whatever to stay as full as possible all the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:06:45-08:00","id":1178221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178120#post1178120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't do Gothic-Punk, though there is nothing wrong with doing so. And you say Trenchcoats and Katanas like it's a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying even full on &quot;I'm Blade&quot; smashing Camarilla/Sabbat with your magical Katana in a Trenchcoat is a political statement. There are no such thing as nonpolitical statements. There is only acknowledging your biases and moving along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's just agree to disagree, shall we? I'm not going to sully myself by arguing over real-life political implications in pretend monster games.<br /> <br /> I don't do the metaplot and I don't do personal horror. I've established this multiple times on this forum since joining back in 2013. </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you use Clans? Sects? Tribes? Traditions? Conventions? KIths? Courts? A simple base &quot;Anarchs vs the world&quot; IS A POLITICAL STATEMENT. A simple &quot;Werewolves vs Pentex&quot; is a political statement. a SImple &quot;mages just trying to survive against the Technocracy&quot; is a political statement. Commoners vs Nobility? Political statement. Nobles vs Nobles Political statement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to turn your campaigns into a political debate team, more power to you. I just want to have fun. The point of gaming is a temporary escape from the burdens of real life. I'm all down for fictional politics in the World of Darkness, but I'll be damned if I drag real-life controversies and political agendas into the gaming table because that's just asking for trouble outside of the game. </div> </div> </div>The Lack of an Agenda is an agenda. The politics of WOD is pretty blatantly baked in. It may be on metaphor and you aren't litterally punching Trump in the face(except when you are because its pure fantasy wishfull fillment). Saying I play an apolitical world of Darkness. Is like saying &quot;I love those Apolitical x-men&quot; even at their silly &quot;space fantasy&quot; level have baked in a story about minorities issues. EVEN OT star wars has politics BAKED in by having evil space wizard facists being fought against by heroic rebels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you must know my political views. I lean left, but not far left. I'm fiscally liberal and socially libertarian. I believe in a strong welfare state founded on mixed market socialism and a democratic republic. I support free speech, free expression, freedom of religion, LGBT rights, and individual liberty. I vehemently oppose extremist and totalitarian ideologies such as Fascism, Nazism, Communism, Theocracy, and Anarchism (the first three ideologies are the tyranny of the state, the other is tyranny of the church, while the last one is the tyranny of mob rule). I am a registered member of the Democratic Party in the Commonwealth of Virginia, and I supported Bernie Sanders in the primaries and voted for Jill Stein in the 2016 election, as I did not want to cast my vote for either Hillary Clinton or Orange Berlusconi.<br /> <br /> So, there. That's my political viewpoint. But I do my best to keep my political life and my gaming life separate. </div> </div> </div>The only part that matters to this discussion is the last statement. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can we please get this discussion back on track? Let's talk about V5, whether it's in support of it or against it, and leave the political debates for the Off-Topic sub-forum. </div> </div> </div>How about this: what separates the World of Darkness from Chronicles of Darkness is a stronger political narrative in the World of Darkness. For example each clan in Requiem is based on a horror genre archtype for the vampire(The Lord, the seducer, the monster, the hoarder of secret knowledge, the beast), while Generally WOD clans more heavily have a political lens, the Brujah vs Ventrue thing as power vs the outsider idealist, but also Ventrue Vs Lasombra a secular vs religious power. <br /> <br /> Since v5 seems to be keeping the clans of Masquerade and focusing EXPLICITLY on Anarch vs Camarilla along with making ABC agencies a major issue for Vampires I don't see how there won't be &quot;Politics baked in&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But yes the Hunger mechanic seems like it will be very annoying in game and very fiddly at least from play tests.(See compromise!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:14:29-08:00","id":1178251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178039#post1178039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason why I post more often at RPG Pub (an explicitly apolitical forum) these days than I do here. I'm tired of all the political debates and controversies. I just want to play my pretend monster games, that's all. It's bad enough that people here give me shit for not playing personal horror. Do we really need to drag real-life politics into this debate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way. But you're not going to find a lot of empathy from people on these forums, as an fyi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:39:08-08:00","id":1178264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178251#post1178251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel the same way. But you're not going to find a lot of empathy from people on these forums, as an fyi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've begun to learn that. But to get on the topic of V5, I am cautiously optimistic about its release. It could be either really good or really bad, and I'm definitely buying it to find out. Worst-case scenario is that if it turns out to be bad, I can mine it for good ideas to put in my 1e and V20 games.<br /> <br /> Fat Larry, you really should join RPG Pub. It's all gaming and no politics and the community is very friendly. If you join up, my name there is Doc Sammy. Tell the mods over there that I sent you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://rpgpub.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpgpub.com</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 01-22-2018, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T17:25:06-08:00","id":1178280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178264#post1178264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've begun to learn that. But to get on the topic of V5, I am cautiously optimistic about its release. It could be either really good or really bad, and I'm definitely buying it to find out. Worst-case scenario is that if it turns out to be bad, I can mine it for good ideas to put in my 1e and V20 games.<br /> <br /> Fat Larry, you really should join RPG Pub. It's all gaming and no politics and the community is very friendly. If you join up, my name there is Doc Sammy. Tell the mods over there that I sent you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://rpgpub.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpgpub.com</a></div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think V5 is LESS politically charged that the variants you have casually dismissed? I mean what we've seen of the changes is a refocusing on the politics of Anarch vs Camarilla. The Sabbat is pulled back. ABC agencies are a threat that have pushed vampires into a corner. That's before we get little bits like the Trans eater of Trump supporters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Similarly as they have moved the Metaplot forward and you have casually rejected such what makes you optimistic?<br /> <br /> Finally the ONLY mechanic we have seen is FAR more intrusive about trying to impose Personal horror than previous versions of Humanity and frenzy? And the power level seems to be pushing downward pulling away from wishfullfillment power fantasy land.<br /> <br /> So tell me what makes you cautiously optimistic? I see nothing in how you have presented yourself that shouldn't make this the thing you have no optimism in. What is the source of your optimism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T17:28:12-08:00","id":1178282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178280#post1178280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you think V5 is LESS politically charged that the variants you have casually dismissed? I mean what we've seen of the changes is a refocusing on the politics of Anarch vs Camarilla. The Sabbat is pulled back. ABC agencies are a threat that have pushed vampires into a corner. That's before we get little bits like the Trans eater of Trump supporters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Similarly as they have moved the Metaplot forward and you have casually rejected such what makes you optimistic?<br /> <br /> Finally the ONLY mechanic we have seen is FAR more intrusive about trying to impose Personal horror than previous versions of Humanity and frenzy? And the power level seems to be pushing downward pulling away from wishfullfillment power fantasy land.<br /> <br /> So tell me what makes you cautiously optimistic? I see nothing in how you have presented yourself that shouldn't make this the thing you have no optimism in. What is the source of your optimism?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The fact that NuWW actually has some semblance of enthusiasm about the project, unlike CCP. Plus, Mark Rein-Hagen is a consultant on the project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T18:10:10-08:00","id":1178296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178282#post1178282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The fact that NuWW actually has some semblance of enthusiasm about the project, unlike CCP. Plus, Mark Rein-Hagen is a consultant on the project.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None of that makes sense. Old WW was pretty damned Enthused about Revised(where you said you jumped out). And the person.. who explicitly wrote multiple tracts on why Gothic Punk gaming is &quot;art&quot; vs &quot;Gaming&quot; and the source of the whole &quot;you are playing the game wrong if you don't include personal horror&quot; makes you feel Optimistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T18:10:20-08:00","id":1178297,"title":"","content":"My two cents about the &quot;political&quot; argument:<br /> <br /> Let's face it, WoD was always political, with a strong leaning to the left. I don't expect it not to be and frankly, I like it for that. One of my main gripes with NWoD back in the day was, that it detached itself too much from the real world. I like very much that WoD is heavily anchored in real-world cultures, cultural phenomenons (including political thoughts and social struggles), mythologies, history and contemporary things, like subcultures. It makes it more immersive and &quot;real&quot; to me. I don't think V5 will be less political, in fact, I think it will be quite (leftist) political. Martin, I think, for example is quite liberal (If I remember correctly, he even talked about how WoD inspired him to learn about leftist political movements and ideologies, when he was younger) and I'd even risk he identifies himself as progressive. Just read some of his facebook posts about GoT, for example.<br /> <br /> What V5 won't do, in my opinion, is tiptoeing around hard topics and catering to certain sensibilities of certain contemporary political groups. Or, to put it bluntly, I expect V5 to be political, even leftist, but I don't expect it to be PC. Some would call that edgy and going for shock value and being heavy-handed and they are being upset about it. Me, I'll welcome it with open arms. Or, to be more precise, welcome back.<br /> <br /> <i>However,</i> I do think WoD could and should be able to be played without always going for real-world political commentary and metaphors. One could totally focus on the supernatural side and internal politics without that. You just don't focus on how some of the splats and factions were being written as real-world metaphors and don't bring real-world political struggles into the game. It'll be there, of course, but you don't have to focus on it.<br /> <br /> Also, about the notion, that every art and in general, everything in life is political... It depends. If you define &quot;political&quot; as everything that got influenced by a certain person's self-identification and worldview, then, yes, sure, everything is political, since it was made/said/done by humans. However, that is not the only, or even the main defintion of the thing. Also, sure, if you're strongly interested in real-life politics, maybe even connected to political and civil groups and you're viewing most of the world through those lenses and participating in pushing the agenda of that group or political side consists a big chung of your life, then, sure, for you, everything will be political and everything will be a part of the real-world political discussion. Simply put: if you feel strongly for a Cause, then it's likely that for you, most things in life will be connected to the Cause or even be about the Cause. The thing is, although, not eveyone sees the world that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T18:23:31-08:00","id":1178300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178282#post1178282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The fact that NuWW actually has some semblance of enthusiasm about the project, unlike CCP. Plus, Mark Rein-Hagen is a consultant on the project.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you hope it will be just more like 1e in the setting, am I right?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it will and won't. Ate least at the beginning.<br /> <br /> - they want to tone down the Camarilla, cities more separated<br /> - want to focus on street-level play<br /> - the Sabbat and the great sect wars will be out, at least, again, at the beginning<br /> - Elders will be mostly out and the remaining quite inhuman<br /> - Anarchs vs. Cam<br /> - core 7 clans at first<br /> <br /> In the meantime:<br /> <br /> - grave wars<br /> - Gehenna happening<br /> - second Inquisition<br /> - definitely want to do metaplot, although they stressed the toned-down importance of signature npcs<br /> <br /> <br /> So, from the point of &quot;how 1e will it be?&quot;, I think it's a mixed bag.<br /> <br /> As for personal horror, I think they'll go for it. However, I don't necessarily see the Hunger mechanics on themselves as making personal horror obligatory. They're just not letting you forget that you're a vampire. How personal horror it will be is more dependant of how the ST handle feeding and relationships with humans and the loss of humanity. In fact, I think the Humanity mechanics will have more to do with how enforced the personal horror will be, than Hunger on itself. Hunger could be totally played, as it stands, as something from an average urban fantasy. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T20:24:17-08:00","id":1178323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178297#post1178297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What V5 won't do, in my opinion, is tiptoeing around hard topics and catering to certain sensibilities of certain contemporary political groups. Or, to put it bluntly, I expect V5 to be political, even leftist, but I don't expect it to be PC. Some would call that edgy and going for shock value and being heavy-handed and they are being upset about it. Me, I'll welcome it with open arms. Or, to be more precise, welcome back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this dichotomy very frustrating. There's this strange idea that you only have two options. You have to &quot;tiptoe&quot; around and be &quot;politically correct,&quot; (though the history of the phrase and how it came to mean how it's commonly used now is strange), or you have to be offensive and outrageous.<br /> <br /> How about we advocate for people just being respectful? One of the things that helped the original WW through some... very poorly written books, is that the company generally was respectful. They made mistakes, but they owned them, and tried to improve. That's all most people actually want. There's some super racist stuff in the WoD books (and not fantasy racism, but real world racism), but the overall trend was to try to correct that, because there's no reason for a gaming book to be perpetuating racist stereotypes of real world groups.<br /> <br /> Acknowledging that, and then actually going better next time? That's good enough for everyone that you should bother counting.<br /> <br /> Saying, &quot;screw that, I'll say what I want, how I want, and I don't care who get's offended,&quot; accomplishes little, and actively hurts minorities when remains a default acceptable stance that doesn't deserve public scorn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, about the notion, that every art and in general, everything in life is political... It depends. If you define &quot;political&quot; as everything that got influenced by a certain person's self-identification and worldview, then, yes, sure, everything is political, since it was made/said/done by humans. However, that is not the only, or even the main defintion of the thing. </div> </div> </div>Way to.... just put words in people's mouths?<br /> <br /> How about this definition: &quot;relating to the government or the public affairs of a country.&quot; It's the first one on Google. That's &quot;main definition&quot; enough, right?<br /> <br /> OK, we're not talking about the government when we're talking about art and entertainment being political. We're walking about &quot;public affairs.&quot; So what's that?<br /> <br /> &quot;(used with a plural verb) matters of general interest or concern, especially those dealing with current social or political issues.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a bit circular, but the social issues part is what matters anyway. The point there is that &quot;everything is political&quot; means that everything (in regards to human creative output) is something that deals with social issues. You can't have an apolitical stance on social issues. Saying, &quot;I don't care about ensuring minority representation in media I create,&quot; is as much a political statement as, &quot;I do care about ensuring minority representation in the media I create.&quot; Because you're making a statement about a social issue: minority representation. That specific issue is way more complicated than just those two positions (avoiding tokenism, appropriation, representation on the creative and management side of things rather than characters, etc.), but there isn't really room for &quot;I don't have a position.&quot; Since that's just, &quot;however things are now is fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply put: if you feel strongly for a Cause, then it's likely that for you, most things in life will be connected to the Cause or even be about the Cause. The thing is, although, not eveyone sees the world that way. </div> </div> </div>And what we're talking about when we say things like &quot;all art is political,&quot; is that &quot;not questioning or seeking to change how things are,&quot; is a Cause even if the people saying it don't see it that way. Not seeing it that way doesn't make it untrue. Not seeing how inaction or refusal to acknowledge a stance is simply empowering the Cause that assumes it speaks for you, it doesn't change what's happening around you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178300#post1178300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for personal horror, I think they'll go for it. However, I don't necessarily see the Hunger mechanics on themselves as making personal horror obligatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue the current Humanity and Hunger rules are actively anti-personal horror (even if that's not the intent). They completely skip any personal horror, because there's no penalty for being a mass murderer to keep your Hunger at zero, for eating rats to avoid harming humans to keep yourself at Hunger 1, and the major consequences of Hunger are random instead of player decision based which detaches players from the horror of what's going on.<br /> <br /> The current Humanity system feels more like &quot;Superman has to go rescue Lois Lane again,&quot; before losing touch with people, instead of, &quot;A monster I am, lest a monster I become.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-22-2018, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T21:10:57-08:00","id":1178332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178297#post1178297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Also, about the notion, that every art and in general, everything in life is political... It depends. If you define &quot;political&quot; as everything that got influenced by a certain person's self-identification and worldview, then, yes, sure, everything is political, since it was made/said/done by humans. However, that is not the only, or even the main defintion of the thing. Also, sure, if you're strongly interested in real-life politics, maybe even connected to political and civil groups and you're viewing most of the world through those lenses and participating in pushing the agenda of that group or political side consists a big chung of your life, then, sure, for you, everything will be political and everything will be a part of the real-world political discussion. Simply put: if you feel strongly for a Cause, then it's likely that for you, most things in life will be connected to the Cause or even be about the Cause. The thing is, although, not eveyone sees the world that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea of making something Apolitical is a political statement. Your biases shape every aspect of your work. Who you cast as heroes and villains is a political statement. Having a hero who comes in and &quot;fixes the system&quot; is a political statement. Yeah some people try to hide their biases and preferences as some concept of neutrality but.. its not true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178300#post1178300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As for personal horror, I think they'll go for it. However, I don't necessarily see the Hunger mechanics on themselves as making personal horror obligatory. They're just not letting you forget that you're a vampire. How personal horror it will be is more dependant of how the ST handle feeding and relationships with humans and the loss of humanity. In fact, I think the Humanity mechanics will have more to do with how enforced the personal horror will be, than Hunger on itself. Hunger could be totally played, as it stands, as something from an average urban fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a much more intrusive form of Frenzy, if you think &quot;losing points on your sheet&quot; is the personal horror of Vampire vs &quot;I murdered a little girl because I was so damned hungry... and she gave me bonuses to surviving this combat...&quot; Yeah.. it supports the idea of &quot;OH MY GOD I AM PLAYING A MONSTER&quot; vs &quot;I'm playing a Dark super hero&quot; everything that throws in your face the monsterous nature of your situation is personal horror. The loss of control is rather key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T21:27:01-08:00","id":1178337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178323#post1178323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'd argue the current Humanity and Hunger rules are actively anti-personal horror (even if that's not the intent). They completely skip any personal horror, because there's no penalty for being a mass murderer to keep your Hunger at zero, for eating rats to avoid harming humans to keep yourself at Hunger 1, and the major consequences of Hunger are random instead of player decision based which detaches players from the horror of what's going on.<br /> <br /> The current Humanity system feels more like &quot;Superman has to go rescue Lois Lane again,&quot; before losing touch with people, instead of, &quot;A monster I am, lest a monster I become.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true I do prefer generally a carrot based method of enagement with issues vs stick but stick has generally been how personal horror has been mechanically circled around as a loss of control by both the player and the character.<br /> <br /> I think perhaps giving mechanical benefits for eating particular humans vs the current situation where there's not but pure fluff keeping a character from not eating a couple hundred rats every night might have some promise on this front but also found that abit lack luster. I think perhaps if the &quot;drinking until you kill someone&quot; level shut down hunger for longer periods of time it might be a worthwhile temptation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T21:46:55-08:00","id":1178342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178323#post1178323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this dichotomy very frustrating. There's this strange idea that you only have two options. You have to &quot;tiptoe&quot; around and be &quot;politically correct,&quot; (though the history of the phrase and how it came to mean how it's commonly used now is strange), or you have to be offensive and outrageous.<br /> <br /> How about we advocate for people just being respectful? One of the things that helped the original WW through some... very poorly written books, is that the company generally was respectful. They made mistakes, but they owned them, and tried to improve. That's all most people actually want. There's some super racist stuff in the WoD books (and not fantasy racism, but real world racism), but the overall trend was to try to correct that, because there's no reason for a gaming book to be perpetuating racist stereotypes of real world groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>When every portrayal of a group or a member of a group in a book, that somebody doesn't like becomes &quot;offensive and outrageous&quot;, or &quot;racist/sexist/xyphobic&quot;, that will get you tiptoeing around topics and groups and yes, into PCism very-very fast. That's the problem. Also, being respectful is good, I'm a big advocate of it and I try to be that. However, it's really hard to be respectful, when every criticism, every kind of non-flattering portrayal got labeled as collectively disrespectful. <br /> <br /> I'm against racism and the other things. Think what you want, I don't really care, I know where I stand. I'm also against the notion that specific groups, cultural issues and such could be portrayed only in a positive way, or in a way that is conforming to certain ideologies. Yes I'm on the side of no &quot;one get a free pass&quot;, when it comes to portrayal in art and media. I want neither overwhelmingly positive (because that's propaganda), nor overwhelmingly negative (because that's hate-mongering) portrayals and I don't believe in taboo topics, because we have to be able to discuss anything. You disagree, you disagree. You do you, I do me. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Acknowledging that, and then actually going better next time? That's good enough for everyone that you should bother counting. </div> </div> </div>Right. And I don't expect WW saying that all assamites are bomb-throwing Middle-Eastern terrorists, or that every Ravnos is a thieving scum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saying, &quot;screw that, I'll say what I want, how I want, and I don't care who get's offended,&quot; accomplishes little, and actively hurts minorities when remains a default acceptable stance that doesn't deserve public scorn. </div> </div> </div>You're entitled to your scorn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Way to.... just put words in people's mouths?<br /> <br /> How about this definition: &quot;relating to the government or the public affairs of a country.&quot; It's the first one on Google. That's &quot;main definition&quot; enough, right?<br /> <br /> OK, we're not talking about the government when we're talking about art and entertainment being political. We're walking about &quot;public affairs.&quot; So what's that? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/political\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/political</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/political\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/languages.oup.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/OL-URL-thumbnail.png?fit=1200%2C627&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/political\" target=\"_blank\"> Oxford Languages </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/political\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/political </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The home of language data. </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/political\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.collinsdictionary.com/di...lish/political</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/political\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.dictionary.com/logo-vocab-com-CKu1F3aD.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/political\" target=\"_blank\"> POLITICAL Definition &amp; Meaning | Dictionary.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/political\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.dictionary.com/browse/political </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> POLITICAL definition: of, relating to, or concerned with politics. See examples of political used in a sentence. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/politics\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/external/images/og-image.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/politics\" target=\"_blank\"> politics </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/politics\" target=\"_blank\"> https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/politics </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> 1. the activities of the government, members of law-making organizations, or&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, the &quot;public affairs&quot; is a part of that, but as you could see in the above links, it's not the first and foremost meaning.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;(used with a plural verb) matters of general interest or concern, especially those dealing with current social or political issues.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a bit circular, but the social issues part is what matters anyway. <b>The point there is that &quot;everything is political&quot; means that everything (in regards to human creative output) is something that deals with social issues.</b> </div> </div> </div>And that is, excuse my french, bullshit. A lot of it is, yes, but not everything. Also a lot of things are <i>inspired </i>by social issues, but not <i>about</i> social issues. Not everything's goal is a political commentary, but some people want to interpret everything as such. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't have an apolitical stance on social issues. Saying, &quot;I don't care about ensuring minority representation in media I create,&quot; is as much a political statement as, &quot;I do care about ensuring minority representation in the media I create.&quot; Because you're making a statement about a social issue: minority representation. That specific issue is way more complicated than just those two positions (avoiding tokenism, appropriation, representation on the creative and management side of things rather than characters, etc.), but there isn't really room for &quot;I don't have a position.&quot; Since that's just, &quot;however things are now is fine.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And that is the problem, because you're confusing portrayal with pushing a narrative, because, I assume, you see <i>every </i>portrayal as pushing <i>someone's</i> narrative. In that worldview, you can't be independent, can't have your own thoughts, you must cater to and be a member of one side or another. You also can't do realistic portrayal, because <i>that</i> will step on someone's toes, because reality is not nice and every side has it's ugliness. Reality isn't any kind of anyone's utopia and <i>I don't think it's art's function or role to make it one</i>. Especially since people can'tagree about how that utopia should look like. A specific artist can push their ideas and wishes, their worldview, nothing's wrong with that, but I don't believe that every art or media should cater to a specific worlview.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what we're talking about when we say things like &quot;all art is political,&quot; is that &quot;not questioning or seeking to change how things are,&quot; is a Cause even if the people saying it don't see it that way. Not seeing it that way doesn't make it untrue. Not seeing how inaction or refusal to acknowledge a stance is simply empowering the Cause that assumes it speaks for you, it doesn't change what's happening around you. </div> </div> </div>You are either with us, or against us, eh? One just can't be impartial, right? If I happen to think vaguely alongside the lines of a group out there about certain topics (but quite disagree with them about others), that doesn't matter, I'm just empowering their Cause. If I'm not rallying behind one Cause that's the same as if I'm rallying behind the opposite Cause, I can't be an individual. You are part of the solution, or part of the problem.<br /> <br /> Well. No. If that is your worldview, be my guest to pursue that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you could say that <i>everything</i> is a Cause, or at least, that everyone has their own peronsal Causes. To some extent, that's right, but it's quite different to seeing and interpreting the world through a political group's narrative constantly and acting upon that.<br /> <br /> And still, not everything in one's life is about social issues, especially the big talking points. At least not for most people.<br /> <br /> One final point about art and politics: my best friend is an electronic composer. He makes a very unique music and has zero interest in making it politically related, in any way. Sure, he doesn't live in a vacuum so, the social environment influences him to a point, but still, his work aren't about those issues pointedly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue the current Humanity and Hunger rules are actively anti-personal horror (even if that's not the intent). They completely skip any personal horror, because there's no penalty for being a mass murderer to keep your Hunger at zero, for eating rats to avoid harming humans to keep yourself at Hunger 1, and the major consequences of Hunger are random instead of player decision based which detaches players from the horror of what's going on. </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd separate the two things. Hunger, as I wrote about, IMO has nothing to do with personal horror and more about reminding the player that she's playing a vampire and adding mechanical and story consequences and quirks to that. It could work perfectly the same way in a more light-hearted game, even in a general fantasy D&amp;D game. Actually, Pathfinder's &quot;Blood of the Night&quot; supplement, which is about playing dhampirs and vampires has something similar. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I have to agree about the latest version of Humantiy in the Alpha. I wrote basically the same to them in the survey. It should be Humanity's role, in conjunction to Hunger, to drive home the personal horror, although the strongest &quot;things&quot; doing it will be always the ST and the layers, regardless of mechanics. Anyway, I agree, the last Humanity rules are actually counterproductive for that. I'd be very surprised if that concept would remain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T21:58:54-08:00","id":1178355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178332#post1178332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The idea of making something Apolitical is a political statement. Your biases shape every aspect of your work. Who you cast as heroes and villains is a political statement. Having a hero who comes in and &quot;fixes the system&quot; is a political statement. Yeah some people try to hide their biases and preferences as some concept of neutrality but.. its not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's a political statement, <i>if</i> you're using it as a political statement (which is a frequent thing and always was), or in the eyes of people, who <i>want </i>to see a political statement in it. Sometimes although, an apple is just an apple is just an apple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its a much more intrusive form of Frenzy, if you think &quot;losing points on your sheet&quot; </div> </div> </div>Or accumulating raises/hunger points...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is the personal horror of Vampire vs &quot;I murdered a little girl because I was so damned hungry... and she gave me bonuses to surviving this combat...&quot; </div> </div> </div>Like usual frenzy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah.. it supports the idea of &quot;OH MY GOD I AM PLAYING A MONSTER&quot; vs &quot;I'm playing a Dark super hero&quot; everything that throws in your face the monsterous nature of your situation is personal horror. The loss of control is rather key. </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. To be fair, <i>some</i> level of personal horror will be always present, if you include any kind of mechanical portrayal of bloodlust, because yeah, taboos of cannibalism and loss of control. However, the Hunger mechanic as it stands, could be rather easily adapted to a Buffyverse game, or Blade, or gods forbid, Anita Blake, or to the White Court of the Dresdenverse. Hunger on itself doesn't make the game deep personal horror, it depends a lot on consequences and actual portrayal. Huinger is just &quot;you're a vamprie, you1re hungry, you do vampire-y things&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T22:00:43-08:00","id":1178356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178342#post1178342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd separate the two things. Hunger, as I wrote about, IMO has nothing to do with personal horror and more about reminding the player that she's playing a vampire and adding mechanical and story consequences and quirks to that. It could work perfectly the same way in a more light-hearted game, even in a general fantasy D&amp;D game. Actually, Pathfinder's &quot;Blood of the Night&quot; supplement, which is about playing dhampirs and vampires has something similar.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I have to agree about the latest version of Humantiy in the Alpha. I wrote basically the same to them in the survey. It should be Humanity's role, in conjunction to Hunger, to drive home the personal horror, although the strongest &quot;things&quot; doing it will be always the ST and the layers, regardless of mechanics. Anyway, I agree, the last Humanity rules are actually counterproductive for that. I'd be very surprised if that concept would remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok maybe we are talking past each other. To me personal horror is.. an internal thing. Slowly going mad, Losing control to inhuman instincts. That a pathfinder game where I had a good chance of freaking out and eating people would contain in my mind &quot;Personal horror&quot; Something that reminds you with regularity &quot;Hey you are a fucking monster&quot;<br /> <br /> What do you see as defining the humanity tract as personal horror? Or do you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T22:15:20-08:00","id":1178360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178356#post1178356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok maybe we are talking past each other. To me personal horror is.. an internal thing. Slowly going mad, Losing control to inhuman instincts. That a pathfinder game where I had a good chance of freaking out and eating people would contain in my mind &quot;Personal horror&quot; Something that reminds you with regularity &quot;Hey you are a fucking monster&quot;<br /> <br /> What do you see as defining the humanity tract as personal horror? Or do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the best I could describe my take on this is this:<br /> <br /> As I wrote above, playing a vampire, with any kind of mechanical and story portrayal of the monstrous parts, meaning, yes, playing a monster and acknowledging that, will always contain a level of personal horror, if the player and ST have even the minimal inclination of going through with it and not brushing it under the carpet.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't make the game a personal horror game in my eyes. It could be a light urban fantasy, for example, with <i>some </i>personal horror elements. What makes a game centered on personal horrors is the actual severity of the vampiric urges and the consequences of those. I'd argue that Hunger is not worse than the old system, it's not more harsh, just more elaborated and adds more quirks to the character. It's level of personal horror, again, depends on actual portrayal at the table, how do you handle feeding and things like that.<br /> <br /> However, the consequences, aka, Humanity is an actual personal horror-stressing element in my eyes. It is literally a mechanic for getting more and more detached and monstrous in general. At least it was, as I said, the current one isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-23-2018, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T23:01:24-08:00","id":1178373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178360#post1178360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the best I could describe my take on this is this:<br /> <br /> As I wrote above, playing a vampire, with any kind of mechanical and story portrayal of the monstrous parts, meaning, yes, playing a monster and acknowledging that, will always contain a level of personal horror, if the player and ST have even the minimal inclination of going through with it and not brushing it under the carpet.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't make the game a personal horror game in my eyes. It could be a light urban fantasy, for example, with <i>some </i>personal horror elements. What makes a game centered on personal horrors is the actual severity of the vampiric urges and the consequences of those. I'd argue that Hunger is not worse than the old system, it's not more harsh, just more elaborated and adds more quirks to the character. It's level of personal horror, again, depends on actual portrayal at the table, how do you handle feeding and things like that.<br /> <br /> However, the consequences, aka, Humanity is an actual personal horror-stressing element in my eyes. It is literally a mechanic for getting more and more detached and monstrous in general. At least it was, as I said, the current one isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that Hunger is far more intrusive as of the last play test and far harder to brush under the carpet. I think its much easier to turn up or down the current frenzy vs from Katanas and Trenchcoats to &quot;OH MY GOD WHAT AM I&quot; while its much harder to extract and control the situation with Hunger.<br /> <br /> Overall I wouldn't say its more penalizing especial from raw but its very much IN YOUR FACE, which is what i find the most annoying about it.<br /> <br /> I don't think personal horror is a &quot;Yes/No&quot; situation but rather degrees, an action game where I'm feeding on bad guys to heal up regularly is a low on personal horror but one where the only choice I have is to hurt fully realized &quot;real&quot; people with bouts of lack of control by the character. The more focus the game gives on the particular horrors of being a vampire the more personal horror it is.<br /> <br /> I would consider playing a Vampire in Dresden Personal Horror. I would consider playing a Vampire in Buffy Personal Horror. And yes I would consider Blade Personal Horror. I wouldn't say consider a Discworld game playing vampires who go to Blood anonymous meetings.. personal horror, or a Demi-chan based slice of life series, or even a &quot;what we do in the shadows' Full on Black Comedy type thing.<br /> <br /> I don't consider the detachment as a consquence all that important or key to personal horror as its never really had any issues outside hitting humanity 0. I am not even sure a system where it would even work unless as you became more and more detached you became less and less able to feed from morally easy prey, like high humanity you can feed from rats, middle humanity you can only feed from people.. but hey you can feed from people you consider scum, low humanity &quot;you can only feed from the innocent&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T00:50:18-08:00","id":1178381,"title":"","content":"Good Lord, what have I done?<br /> <br /> Guys, let's just agree to disagree on this issue and leave it at that. I apologize for ever bringing this up in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T03:17:42-08:00","id":1178392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178337#post1178337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true I do prefer generally a carrot based method of enagement with issues vs stick but stick has generally been how personal horror has been mechanically circled around as a loss of control by both the player and the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before even getting to carrots and sticks, there's the issue of player input. The alpha V5 rules are very much, &quot;roll to see if being a vampire randomly sucks today.&quot; There's nothing you as the player, or your character can really do about this. You just randomly messy crit, or get blood hungry as the dice decide regardless of what you do or don't do besides killing people. When the only meaningful choice is, &quot;do I kill humans when I need Hunger 0&quot; or not, you're going to lose anything close to personal horror.<br /> <br /> If the keystone to personal horror is, &quot;what have I become?&quot; moments, than V5 loses the point because it starts you past the point of having those. V5 characters as they stand now are already psychologically accepting seeing humans as a resource to abuse for controlling their own supernatural hunger. Feeding on blood is no more horrific for them than my need to cook a meal. We're just in straight supernatural horror where people are playing the monsters.<br /> <br /> Carrots and sticks both have their place, but the important thing is that they work together towards creating the play experience the designers are aiming for. Hunger's carrots and sticks before even looking at how Humanity operates are all over the place. It doesn't guide players towards, well, anything, because the effects are too random to do much more than wait to see how mean/nice the dice are going to be tonight. It reminds you that your character is a vampire a lot, without reminding you that vampires are monsters much at all.<br /> <br /> Then the new Humanity rules get added to that, and fail to add meaningful guidance as well. So we get the two systems that are core to framing the horror of the game.. not really framing anything.<br /> <br /> The VtM Humanity system is annoying stick-only, and frustratingly written in any number of ways, but for the most part it keeps to the goal of what the mechanics are trying to reinforce. The biggest problem is that Virtues work in a counter-intuitive way towards their descriptions; which is to say they don't help you resist temptation like that say they do, but instead help you resist the consequences of giving in. So instead of a high Conscience character not avoiding doing bad things because they're compassionate and connected to their human empathy, they can do more bad things because their moral integrity resists Degeneration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178342#post1178342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When every portrayal of a group or a member of a group in a book, that somebody doesn't like becomes &quot;offensive and outrageous&quot;, or &quot;racist/sexist/xyphobic&quot;, that will get you tiptoeing around topics and groups and yes, into PCism very-very fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>A worry I've heard expressed very frequently, but actualized in the artistic/entertainment world pretty much... never? Where is this meaningful consensus by.... anyone... that even portraying X is inherently offensive or outrageous? There's lots debate on the Internet of individual instances of portrayals being offensive or not... but the only people I can think of that actually flat out say portraying a given X in any fashion are small groups of religious fundamentalists. And I don't generally see artists caving to those in the big picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also against the notion that specific groups, cultural issues and such could be portrayed only in a positive way, or in a way that is conforming to certain ideologies. </div> </div> </div>But this inherently butts against being respectful in a bad way. There is a 100+ year history of black men in film being portrayed as violent thugs, and more recent trends of things like the token black character, or the &quot;black dude dies first&quot; trope. Do black men get a free pass in all art and entertainment? Of course not. But if you don't respect that history when creating a negative portrayal (or better a complex portrayal) of a black man, then you're not being respectful at a minimum, and you're easily getting towards doing something racist. Samuel L Jackson alone has played a huge number of villain/antagonist/negative black characters, and a bunch more deeply flawed characters that aren't part of the protagonist/antagonist setup of a film, and you don't see a lot of falling for the tired and offensive tropes of portrayals of black men in film going back to 1915. You can do Mr. Glass (Unbreakable), Richmond Valetine (Kingsmen), Preston Packard (Kong: Skull Island), Barron (Mrs. Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children), and Stepthen the house slave (Django Unchained) all without getting slammed for being racist despite black men doing either overtly evil, or just idiotic in the face of facts bad, things.<br /> <br /> Being respectful (that thing you said you're all for) does mean thinking about how your portray people in fiction in both their personal context, and the larger social issues involved. It means acting on it too.<br /> <br /> You can't be respectful and avoid conforming to certain ideologies in how to portray people in fiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and I don't believe in taboo topics, because we have to be able to discuss anything. </div> </div> </div>But, again, as a matter of respect, you have to acknowledge that there are times and places for certain topics. And while the wider world of art might be able to handle discussing anything, a RPG book might never be a good place for certain discussions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right. And I don't expect WW saying that all assamites are bomb-throwing Middle-Eastern terrorists, or that every Ravnos is a thieving scum. </div> </div> </div>Based on what we've seen from them so far... I'm not confident it even that at all. WW has already floated the idea that the unrest in the Middle East since after 2001 is because some massive number of the Sabbat went there for Antedeluvian something something reasons. The Mage Prelude paints the Technocracy as supporting anti-immigration right-wing fascists. So... yeah... the track record so far on treating the interaction of supernaturals and real world people is not confidence building to me in the slightest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also a lot of things are <i>inspired </i>by social issues, but not <i>about</i> social issues. Not everything's goal is a political commentary, but some people want to interpret everything as such. </div> </div> </div>See this might be part of the problem. You're assuming that we're trying to say that everything's goal is to be political commentary. But you might notice that wasn't what was said. Just that there's political aspects to the work in question.<br /> <br /> When I'm inspired by social issues to design my game worlds with a better eye towards minority representation than I did when I was a kid, I'm trying to make a game world that's more fun to play in because it's more authentic. I'm not trying to make commentary about media representation, or the treatment of minorities. But that was a political decision on my part, that's about a social issue. It means there's politics in my gaming decisions. It's really that simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that is the problem, because you're confusing portrayal with pushing a narrative, because, I assume, you see <i>every </i>portrayal as pushing <i>someone's</i> narrative. </div> </div> </div>All art and entertainment are forms of communication of a narrative from the creators to the audience. Portrayals are part of the language of artistic communication... so yes? How a creator chooses to portray a character is inherently part of how they communicate their narrative.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how this is even an issue for debate or a matter of perspective. What is a character doing if their portrayal isn't communicating a narrative for the creator?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that worldview, you can't be independent, can't have your own thoughts, you must cater to and be a member of one side or another. </div> </div> </div>Seriously... what the actual fuck?<br /> <br /> Who said anything of the sort?<br /> <br /> This is a complete non-sequitur. How does, &quot;art inherently involves the communication of ideas, so characters are inherently aspects of their creator's narrative,&quot; turn into, &quot;you can't have your own thoughts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, to an extent, no man is an island. But you're taking that to an extreme unsaid and disrespectful of what I'm trying to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A specific artist can push their ideas and wishes, their worldview, nothing's wrong with that, but I don't believe that every art or media should cater to a specific worlview. </div> </div> </div>And.. you do realize that the whole point here is only that every artist is pushing their ideas into their work... right? That's all. None of this divisive bullshit that you keep piling on with no basis to the idea being discussed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are either with us, or against us, eh? One just can't be impartial, right? </div> </div> </div>So... respectful to you means... when you disagree with someone, the best thing to do is respond with comments that are only designed to misrepresent what people are saying, since respect is all about trying your hardest to make other people look bad in a conversation... and never honestly engaging with what they said?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, you could say that <i>everything</i> is a Cause, or at least, that everyone has their own peronsal Causes. To some extent, that's right, but it's quite different to seeing and interpreting the world through a political group's narrative constantly and acting upon that. </div> </div> </div>And the first part? That's what I'm actually talking about. The second part? That's bullshit you're adding for no positive reason. You keep trying to tack on &quot;political groups&quot; to the idea that art is inherently political. Stop it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And still, not everything in one's life is about social issues, especially the big talking points. At least not for most people. </div> </div> </div>Again, there's a difference between feeling it's a part of your life, and it actually being a part of your life.<br /> <br /> Allow me to paraphrase Anthony Bourdain in a recent spot on a late night talk show. Bourdain's a famous chef, a the culinary world is a horror show of sexism. Bourdain's a complete asshole (though he does own it) but he always thought of himself as someone that treated people equally without regard for things like gender or sex (and by all accounts that's true). But during the whole #metoo thing he realized something. Despite years and years of not feeling his life was about sexual harassment because he was one of the good guys, he self reflected and realized that not a single woman that he's worked with that has come out with a story ever trusted him enough to confide in him. All of his self image about how he'd never stand for that crap, and he was above it, was shattered by the fact that he never put in the work to be worth telling, so he never had to do the work of calling people out from his position of power.<br /> <br /> These things are all around us, every day, everywhere. Humans are social animals. We live in social units and we build up societies. What happens in those overlapping social circles we occupy is part of our lives. And we all own how much attention we pay to it, and what we do about it. That ownership might be individualistic, but it's not free from interconnectivity either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd separate the two things. Hunger, as I wrote about, IMO has nothing to do with personal horror and more about reminding the player that she's playing a vampire and adding mechanical and story consequences and quirks to that. It could work perfectly the same way in a more light-hearted game, even in a general fantasy D&amp;D game. Actually, Pathfinder's &quot;Blood of the Night&quot; supplement, which is about playing dhampirs and vampires has something similar. </div> </div> </div>Sure, though I maintain the randomness of it and lack of player agency is a problem independent of Humanity and genre/playstyle. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, I agree, the last Humanity rules are actually counterproductive for that. I'd be very surprised if that concept would remain. </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm not sure where this confidence is coming from. I think the Humanity rules will get refined and probably be less dumb. But I don't see why WW is going to abandon the odd focus on a Touchstone thing. Nothing seems to indicate they plan on moving away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T08:46:40-08:00","id":1178445,"title":"","content":"On an earlier point I made. <br /> Yes, dominate ain't supposed to use blood. Most use of disciplines don't use blood. Animalism? no. Auspex? no.Obfuscate? no. Fortitude? no. Potence? Mostly no.<br /> Celerity and presence? A lot, but there's <i>a reason </i> for that. <br /> <br /> In simple terms, disciplines are an aspect of mastery. Imagine a vampire as a professional or just a person of society. If people or animals see themselves as subordinate to you, they obey you, you don't need to spend resources to compel them to do something, they obey. Meanwhile, obfuscate works on the logic that people don't want to see what's there, they don't want to see the true face of a nosferatu, they're happier to see the nicer face being worn, they're willfully ignorant. Presence, on the other hand, mostly uses blood, and that's because emotional manipulation crosses status lines, Flattery is a bribe and drawing people to you involves resources. Celerity, well, it costs a lot to rush... <br /> <br /> There's a statement there, in the disciplines, about human nature. Just hand waving all that and having every dot cost blood regardless is a murder of commentary (it also kills all the nosferatu)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:28:04-08:00","id":1178552,"title":"","content":"That seems... really forced. It certainly not something the creators of the game or later developers have stated.<br /> <br /> There's also some holes in the theory as an emergent property. Dominate doesn't care if people see you as a superior or not. You don't have to spend blood on Dominate if someone thinks they're superior to you. A character doing the lord of the sewers or back alleys thing that looks like a bum can still Dominate cops and rich people that feel they have authority or social power over them. A neonate can Dominate a Prince if Generation doesn't get in the way.<br /> <br /> Presence, Dementation, and Chimestry all have blood costs whether you're using them to violate status lines or not. Obfuscate (esp. Mask of 1K Faces) can be used to cross status lines by convincing people you're someone of higher status. There isn't an optional blood cost in Mask of 1K Faces to impersonate a Primogen and try to violate social conventions and order people around. It's only for overcoming a difference in Appearance between you and your Mask.<br /> <br /> If this is all about mastery, why does mastery over the body (Vicissitude or Protean) cost blood? A Tzimisce lord over their ghouls still pays blood to assert that mastery physically. A Gangrel's mastery of their own body doesn't let them shapeshift without cost.<br /> <br /> Why does Necromancy sometimes cost blood and sometimes not... while Thaumaturgy always does in this framework?<br /> <br /> It seems there's as many counter points to this as there are supporting points.<br /> <br /> I can't really think of any consistent framework for in-character explanations of why some Disciplines are blood heavy and others aren't. It's not &quot;physical vs mental,&quot; because a bunch of mental powers are blood heavy, and some of the physical orient ones aren't, and whatever you want to do with the more esoteric ones.<br /> <br /> Even the Nosferatu point is diminished by the fact that they need to spend at least one blood point to create a Mask that'll make them humanly ugly to walk around humans with even if the power doesn't usually cost blood.<br /> <br /> If the game designers for VtM want to make a serious commentary about human nature via what costs blood and what doesn't... the Disciplines need a huge re-write. I really can't see a case for anything other than the blood cost being much more game and much less purposefully commentary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:19:48-08:00","id":1178667,"title":"","content":"Heavy arms, I think we may be talking past eachother. I don't particularly think Hunger is a good mechanic. I feel its increadibly intrusive. I however DO think its INTENT is to be intrusive about Personal Horror. I don't think its going to work so well ultimately and tests have shown its.. really just &quot;This is fucking annoying.. roll more dice to pull me out of the situation.&quot; its.. very overt in your face mechanic.<br /> <br /> Vs Frenzy, humanity all that which is even by Raw far less in your face and generally easier to house rule up or down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T02:57:01-08:00","id":1178709,"title":"","content":"Yeah, probably. The big point I'm trying to make is that the intrusiveness isn't necessarily a problem. Some people mind intrusiveness more than others, and for some aspects of the game more than others. Satiety from BtP is my go to example for how I think you can do the same concept well, and it's pretty intrusive. But the player gets to decide if they want to teeter on the edge of starving for the free power boost and simple feeding, to focus on psychological powers and intense feeding with the risk of overfeeding and being at your weakest, or risking the middle so you can try to jump to either side as you want.<br /> <br /> It's the level of choice that I think's really important to getting personal horror to work, and what I feel the Hunger rules lack more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T04:17:07-08:00","id":1178720,"title":"","content":"While you may say that a man in rags can dominate someone in a business suit, the dude in rags is a vampire, he's above people by merit of being a vampire, even if the person totally lacks the awareness talent, I'm sure dominate throws enough into the soul for the thing to work.The mentioned neonate's going to have a hard roll on the prince, but do remember how the flaw &quot;laughingstock&quot; damages your ability to use the power. With mask of the thousand faces, people are just more willing to pretend they're dealing with someone of the appropriate status lines (also, being a vampire is a big metaphysical plus) <br /> <br /> For your second point, mastery/rare disciplines using blood makes total sense. <br /> Thaumaturges are sacrificing blood for miracles to happen. Assamite sorcerers, depending on the book you read, are downright paying spirits to work their magic for them. <br /> For protean, well you're literally paying to create or convert matter. It's almost obvious it wouldn't be free. <br /> <br /> Basically, some disciplines have a metaphysical reason to always be free of blood expenditure, others have reasons to always use blood expenditure. It's very simple, and you might have one or two &quot;but what if...&quot; but overall, things point one way or another, and most certainly you can't just have an all or none approach to different disciplines using blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:10:26-08:00","id":1178751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178709#post1178709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, probably. The big point I'm trying to make is that the intrusiveness isn't necessarily a problem. Some people mind intrusiveness more than others, and for some aspects of the game more than others. Satiety from BtP is my go to example for how I think you can do the same concept well, and it's pretty intrusive. But the player gets to decide if they want to teeter on the edge of starving for the free power boost and simple feeding, to focus on psychological powers and intense feeding with the risk of overfeeding and being at your weakest, or risking the middle so you can try to jump to either side as you want.<br /> <br /> It's the level of choice that I think's really important to getting personal horror to work, and what I feel the Hunger rules lack more than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Definately like the way you are describing the situation, but I do think that the intrusiveness of Hunger is an issue in and of itself. Every action.. even non &quot;empowered' actions have a chance of setting it off. I would think if the Hunger dice were a benefit rather than something that happens naturally that it was something you could turn on for benefits(and costs!) but something you could attempt to avoid more readily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T17:59:41-08:00","id":1179031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178720#post1178720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you may say that a man in rags can dominate someone in a business suit, the dude in rags is a vampire, he's above people by merit of being a vampire, even if the person totally lacks the awareness talent, I'm sure dominate throws enough into the soul for the thing to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is inconsistent with you own logic the Dominate doesn't cost blood to use because it's about the exercise of authority, while Presence costs blood because it's about violating social positions.<br /> <br /> If humans are innately &quot;below&quot; vampires, then Presence use on them isn't a violation of any social hierarchy and shouldn't cost blood. Presence powers would have no-blood clauses to use on humans, and blood costing clauses to use on vampires. But that's not how the rules work at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mentioned neonate's going to have a hard roll on the prince, but do remember how the flaw &quot;laughingstock&quot; damages your ability to use the power. </div> </div> </div>The difficulty of Dominate rolls (at least that apply to another vampires) have a base of the target's current Willpower. Even a Willpower 10 Prince can be under enough pressure for that difficulty to drop low enough they can be Dominated with ease. The neonate just needs to wait (or arrange) for the Prince to be emotionally drained and the rolls gets easy.<br /> <br /> Dominate - besides the Generation protection - is never about actual relative social standing between characters, but about the target's mentality. The target's will matters, the target's Nature matters, the target's opinion of the user might matter (though that Flaw is a strange addition to something that doesn't otherwise exist in Dominate), but the relative social standing between the two never matters. Which means your initial assertion about the metaphysical themes of Disciplines is suspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With mask of the thousand faces, people are just more willing to pretend they're dealing with someone of the appropriate status lines (also, being a vampire is a big metaphysical plus) </div> </div> </div>Except the &quot;willingness&quot; of people never matters to the power. The difficulty is normally static unless trying to impersonate a specific person without time to study them, the successes dictate how successful the mask you create is to viewers, and the blood cost is always based on the difference between what you are and what you're trying to disguise yourself to be instead of the perceptions of others.<br /> <br /> You keep adding things to these powers that aren't there to try to say there's an emergent narrative within them. Nothing in Obfuscate cares about what people want to believe or playing into preconceptions like that. Vanish From The Mind's Eye is actually pretty likely to leave a sizeable minority portion of mortals with an obvious memory of a supernatural act (the vampire up and disappearing) than leave them filling in the blanks to pretend nothing happened. Playing towards people's preconceptions never matters, the targets' base traits (for difficulty) and Willpower (for remembering or not) is what matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thaumaturges are sacrificing blood for miracles to happen. </div> </div> </div>Why don't all the &quot;miracles&quot; of necromancers cost blood then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For protean, well you're literally paying to create or convert matter. It's almost obvious it wouldn't be free. </div> </div> </div>That's not an explanation within the narrative you're saying the Disciplines create. How does spending blood to violate the laws of physics play into the social narrative you're claiming is vital to protect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, some disciplines have a metaphysical reason to always be free of blood expenditure, others have reasons to always use blood expenditure. It's very simple, and you might have one or two &quot;but what if...&quot; but overall, things point one way or another, and most certainly you can't just have an all or none approach to different disciplines using blood. </div> </div> </div>How many &quot;but what if...&quot; exceptions apply before it's clear the framework you're claiming exists doesn't bear out to be solid?<br /> <br /> Why can't you have an all or none approach to Disciplines using blood... especially if you're writing a never version of the game and might want to adjust any emergent statements of how Discipline use impacts vampires?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1178751#post1178751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Definately like the way you are describing the situation, but I do think that the intrusiveness of Hunger is an issue in and of itself. Every action.. even non &quot;empowered' actions have a chance of setting it off. I would think if the Hunger dice were a benefit rather than something that happens naturally that it was something you could turn on for benefits(and costs!) but something you could attempt to avoid more readily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess my question to this is, if you thought a mechanic was fun (so ignoring that at least the current Hunger rules aren't to at least some of us, and definitely the two of us) would the level of intrusiveness that Hunger has still bother you? If you liked the outcomes of &quot;any roll could result in X coming out,&quot; isn't not really a problem is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:36:46-08:00","id":1179077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179031#post1179031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I guess my question to this is, if you thought a mechanic was fun (so ignoring that at least the current Hunger rules aren't to at least some of us, and definitely the two of us) would the level of intrusiveness that Hunger has still bother you? If you liked the outcomes of &quot;any roll could result in X coming out,&quot; isn't not really a problem is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I Guess if it were an engaging and fun mechanic I wouldn't find it intrusive. Its not even the &quot;anything could happen&quot; aspect of it so much as.. ITS IN EVERY ROLL. Every roll has to engage in.. looking around the room? Have to engage in it, not passions, not hunger, not using powers.. every damned thing.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:55:16-08:00","id":1179087,"title":"","content":"Cool, then I think we're basically on the same page then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T05:38:05-08:00","id":1179496,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping V5 is more supportive of different play-styles like 1e, 2e, and V20 were and that they don't take the &quot;One True Way&quot; approach regarding personal horror that Revised took.<br /> <br /> I mean, if Personal Horror is present as one of many equally valid play-styles (as it was in 1e and 2e) that's cool and all, but I don't want NuWW telling me I'm playing the game wrong just because I'm not playing their specific preferred way.<br /> <br /> That whole &quot;you're playing the game wrong&quot; and &quot;Go Play Some Other Game&quot; attitude is very condescending and it really rubs me the wrong way. As long as everyone's having fun, does it really matter how the game is being played?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:42:30-08:00","id":1179539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179496#post1179496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping V5 is more supportive of different play-styles like 1e, 2e, and V20 were and that they don't take the &quot;One True Way&quot; approach regarding personal horror that Revised took.<br /> <br /> I mean, if Personal Horror is present as one of many equally valid play-styles (as it was in 1e and 2e) that's cool and all, but I don't want NuWW telling me I'm playing the game wrong just because I'm not playing their specific preferred way.<br /> <br /> That whole &quot;you're playing the game wrong&quot; and &quot;Go Play Some Other Game&quot; attitude is very condescending and it really rubs me the wrong way. As long as everyone's having fun, does it really matter how the game is being played?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that back in the old editions, you'd get a scolding, but the mechanics wouldn't really change to prevent you from playing that way. From what we've seen of the incoming edition, ParaWolf is angling to do the opposite, skipping the lecture and just making it mechanically untenable to play that way. Keep in mind that one of the people that they brought on to create the game, Kenneth Hite, has expressed a profound distaste in letting people play vampires, and his prior project, Night's Black Agents, was about playing burned spies who hunt vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:35:29-08:00","id":1179593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179539#post1179539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that back in the old editions, you'd get a scolding, but the mechanics wouldn't really change to prevent you from playing that way. From what we've seen of the incoming edition, ParaWolf is angling to do the opposite, skipping the lecture and just making it mechanically untenable to play that way. Keep in mind that one of the people that they brought on to create the game, Kenneth Hite, has expressed a profound distaste in letting people play vampires, and his prior project, Night's Black Agents, was about playing burned spies who hunt vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> God, I hope they don't go through with that for the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T14:22:55-08:00","id":1179614,"title":"","content":"Hite's comments on playing vampires are a bit messy. NBA has a sidebar about how playing &quot;good&quot; vampires is dumb, but also includes rules for them anyway. He's never had a problem writing for the WoD in the past, probably because vampires in the WoD are generally horrible people; even the ones trying to be good. He's also publicly commented about how to mesh his side-bar in NBA with having a lead position on V5... that personally comes off as kinda wishy-washy to me. Basically, I think that as pointed out V5's baked in Hunger system is going to make V5 far too mechanically invested in a single playstyle (one that Hite is OK with for playable vampires) to be worth getting for someone looking for a more easily hacked core rules if you want to do something else with it (though there's also plenty of those around as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:10:42-08:00","id":1179649,"title":"","content":"I like playing heroic vampires, and if what you guys are saying is true, then I might give V5 a pass after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:52:04-08:00","id":1179738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179496#post1179496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping V5 is more supportive of different play-styles like 1e, 2e, and V20 were and that they don't take the &quot;One True Way&quot; approach regarding personal horror that Revised took.<br /> <br /> I mean, if Personal Horror is present as one of many equally valid play-styles (as it was in 1e and 2e) that's cool and all, but I don't want NuWW telling me I'm playing the game wrong just because I'm not playing their specific preferred way.<br /> <br /> That whole &quot;you're playing the game wrong&quot; and &quot;Go Play Some Other Game&quot; attitude is very condescending and it really rubs me the wrong way. As long as everyone's having fun, does it really matter how the game is being played?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I've never felt that 1e or 2e were particularly less lecturey about &quot;Bad wrong fun&quot; than Revised. Now Revised seems to have more lectures on some of the Emergent playstyle that came out of 1e and 2e but there's plenty of &quot;This isn't D&amp;D&quot; and &quot;Deep personal horror&quot; statements in 1e and 2e books.(Aberrant however wins this for all of WW books because it actually has this essay explicit)<br /> <br /> I am honestly not sure you can make a game that serves everyone equally well, but that doesn't mean there shouldn't be Heroic Vampire games. Or games where you are the heroic vampire as part of the resistance to the evil overlords who secretly run everything or variants there in. a &quot;Vampire:Action!&quot; wouldn't be a bad game. It would actually be a pretty awesome game in my mind, a subtle refocusing towards a more over the top cinematic setting while keeping much of the same players and powers..<br /> <br /> Might be something to Storyteller Vault out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T22:51:21-08:00","id":1179757,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that once Scion 2e and Trinity 2e are out, we'll have a good system (for those that like the ST base system concepts) to do homebrew conversions of the WoD games to something more action/adventure oriented. The mechanics are similar enough that porting things shouldn't be hard, and Storypath is designed to handle high powered games much better than the WoD systems are without breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T00:46:04-08:00","id":1179773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179757#post1179757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that once Scion 2e and Trinity 2e are out, we'll have a good system (for those that like the ST base system concepts) to do homebrew conversions of the WoD games to something more action/adventure oriented. The mechanics are similar enough that porting things shouldn't be hard, and Storypath is designed to handle high powered games much better than the WoD systems are without breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its an option as well, I just think with the options ST Vault allows a rule set variant that is tuned with different degrees might be a popular addition there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T01:42:16-08:00","id":1179776,"title":"","content":"Probably? For those of us not in the mood to give even more money to WW than whatever portion of buying OP products goes to covering the licensing fee, the ST Vault isn't really a great option.<br /> <br /> As well, as far as I understand it, the ST Vault doesn't allow the level of modification I think the WoD would need to tune it to a really fun action oriented system. The amount of complexity Exalted 3e has to go through just to make a good swashbuckling style fight work on the Storyteller chassis is pretty evident of the amount of work I'd want to see done... and fortunately OP already did a pretty impressive job of it with Storypath IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T02:58:07-08:00","id":1179780,"title":"","content":"It's likely just me, but I never got the &quot;personal horror&quot; vibe from Vampire. Political horror is a whole other beast though: the internal conflicts within the Camarilla, the intersect strife between the Camarilla, Sabbat and Anarchs and all of that paired with the approaching Gehenna and the various other horrors at work means that the whole personal horror thing is put in the background a bit. That's not to say that there isn't a Vampire game that does not play with personal horror, it's just that this game is Vampire: The Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T07:20:01-08:00","id":1179822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179773#post1179773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its an option as well, I just think with the options ST Vault allows a rule set variant that is tuned with different degrees might be a popular addition there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For sure. And I know a number of really good people who have some material on there that I've gladly supported. I think a variant would work really well on the STV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T07:45:21-08:00","id":1179825,"title":"","content":"I have been drafting ideas for material to submit to the Storyteller's Vault, so why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:24:40-08:00","id":1179920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179776#post1179776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably? For those of us not in the mood to give even more money to WW than whatever portion of buying OP products goes to covering the licensing fee, the ST Vault isn't really a great option.<br /> <br /> As well, as far as I understand it, the ST Vault doesn't allow the level of modification I think the WoD would need to tune it to a really fun action oriented system. The amount of complexity Exalted 3e has to go through just to make a good swashbuckling style fight work on the Storyteller chassis is pretty evident of the amount of work I'd want to see done... and fortunately OP already did a pretty impressive job of it with Storypath IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not about giving WW more money its about giving someone who does alot of work some money for it. And if it gets noticed maybe it might get more official backing and people can get there nice book hardcover books too. I want everyone to have their options.<br /> <br /> As for how hard it is to make Storyteller into something more action, yes that's the case.. but its also going to be quite abit of work converting the various vampiric powers, balancing them for the sort of story etc. Its going to be alot of work across the board no matter what you do so I'd like to be able to say to a person who works it out more than &quot;Good job&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:25:34-08:00","id":1179936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179780#post1179780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's likely just me, but I never got the &quot;personal horror&quot; vibe from Vampire. Political horror is a whole other beast though: the internal conflicts within the Camarilla, the intersect strife between the Camarilla, Sabbat and Anarchs and all of that paired with the approaching Gehenna and the various other horrors at work means that the whole personal horror thing is put in the background a bit. That's not to say that there isn't a Vampire game that does not play with personal horror, it's just that this game is Vampire: The Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtM suffered heavily from being the first. WW was still throwing whatever ideas at the wall and just seeing what stuck. The political aspect of VtM was a huge aesthetic element that helped it stand out from previous vampire fiction, and to an extent a lot of RPGs (most RPGs kept the PCs out of politics completely, or kept them on the lower side of them for various reasons, rather than make political climbing a real way to approach things).<br /> <br /> VtM still wanted to be personal horror though, and has plenty of elements of that in the game.<br /> <br /> VtR continues the desire to be personal horror with vampires... with 23 years of VtM to help it refocus (and then even more experience for VtR 2e). It's definitely a better personal horror game.. but that doesn't mean VtM doesn't have it as a significant part of play; at least as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179920#post1179920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not about giving WW more money...</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on your position on things... if you don't want to give WW money directly, the ST Vault is a 50/50 split between the creator and WW... so you're giving WW money. Sure, it's also good that companies are starting to let people profit off of their quality fan creations, but you can't just separate on from the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if it gets noticed maybe it might get more official backing and people can get there nice book hardcover books too. </div> </div> </div>Lets not sell these things as more than what they are. Maybe someone gets noticed... but these programs aren't about building new RPG creators by giving them a chance to make their own books to prove what they can do. It's about monetizing fan creations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:36:51-08:00","id":1179941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179936#post1179936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That depends on your position on things... if you don't want to give WW money directly, the ST Vault is a 50/50 split between the creator and WW... so you're giving WW money. Sure, it's also good that companies are starting to let people profit off of their quality fan creations, but you can't just separate on from the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can prioritize. I'd like to give someone some sort of financial reward for the LARGE amount of hard work that will be employed. Yes its 50 percent going to WW... but that's more than &quot;Nothing&quot; the fan would be getting for releasing it for free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lets not sell these things as more than what they are. Maybe someone gets noticed... but these programs aren't about building new RPG creators by giving them a chance to make their own books to prove what they can do. It's about monetizing fan creations.<br /> </div> </div> </div>We can all agree there is a largely unfillfilled market out there of WOD fans who want a more action &quot;Heroic&quot; type game than is traditionally presented by the book and that V5 definately seems to be moving away from if Hunger is any indication.<br /> <br /> So there's a market that deserves filling, STV has the best chance of allowing those who want something like that and getting a nice thick printed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:45:49-08:00","id":1179957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179936#post1179936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets not sell these things as more than what they are. Maybe someone gets noticed... but these programs aren't about building new RPG creators by giving them a chance to make their own books to prove what they can do. It's about monetizing fan creations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is funny. I know your position is usually that of contrarian corner...on everything. But on this? I really did lol.<br /> <br /> The two are not mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> Most of the writers who were employed by Onyx Path and White Wolf were fans first. Many of them were forum users. Like yourself.<br /> <br /> The Storytellers Vault IS giving fans the outlet to do something they love, maybe get noticed by someone in the industry(and at the same time, building their own resume), with ANOTHER positive of actually making a little bit of money to do so.<br /> <br /> There are really no negatives to it, from my perspective. But you go on ahead, stick it to the White Wolf man!<br /> <br /> Go get 'em!<br /> <br /> I--and many others, will continue to support our fellow gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T17:34:26-08:00","id":1179990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179941#post1179941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can prioritize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said otherwise. I just said that the ST Vault isn't a great option for people that prioritize differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We can all agree there is a largely unfillfilled market out there of WOD fans who want a more action &quot;Heroic&quot; type game than is traditionally presented by the book and that V5 definately seems to be moving away from if Hunger is any indication. </div> </div> </div>And the ST Vault content guidelines don't really indicate that this sort of product would be allowed there... not to mention just supporting smaller game publishers that have already made games for this market. The guidelines say things need to stay in-theme with VtM (specifically using changing the genre to things like steampunk or post-apocalyptic as examples) as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So there's a market that deserves filling, STV has the best chance of allowing those who want something like that and getting a nice thick printed book. </div> </div> </div>They can't get a physical book. OBS's community content programs don't allow PoD services. You can only upload digital files like PDFs and STLs (3D printer files). No amount of supporting the ST Vault is going to change that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1179957#post1179957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know your position is usually that of contrarian corner...on everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know that you're fully embracing the modern conservative approach of making ad hominem comments to try to discredit people you disagree with rather than paying attention to what they say; and of course complaining that you don't get enough &quot;empathy&quot; for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The two are not mutually exclusive. </div> </div> </div>Never said they were. But the goal of the ST Vault is not to promote fans to employees. It isn't designed for it, and trying to promote it with the idea that &quot;you might be discovered and hired by the company!&quot; is highly misleading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the writers who were employed by Onyx Path and White Wolf were fans first. Many of them were forum users. Like yourself. </div> </div> </div>The results of which have been a fairly mixed bag (esp. for those people).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are really no negatives to it, from my perspective.... </div> </div> </div>My big issue with the general concept (as opposed to The ST Vault in particular)? It perpetuates a business model that tries to get as much content as possible while providing as little pay as possible. Instead of putting effort into showing how, you know, paying more money for the basic books so the writers and freelance developers can get paid decently for their work is supporting our fellow gamers, we're being sold on supporting our fellow gamers by tipping them for their work (since they generally make even less than freelancers for even more work, that's still taxable).<br /> <br /> I'd rather my gaming money go towards keeping skilled RPG creators working on the properties I love, so they have time to help the next generation rather than needing to go have a real job or work on another three projects to pay the bills. Constantly replacing freelancers from a pool of fans because it turns out most of them aren't really up for doing it professionally for any number of reasons, isn't a good model for the hobby or the industry.<br /> <br /> Continuity of experience beats grinding out replaceable freelancers in the long run every time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T17:49:01-08:00","id":1179992,"title":"","content":"There are people who like bits of hte background and cosmology, I can't make an action game for example with Caine as the first vampire, 13 clans, I mean Trenchcoats and Katanas exists.. but its very much itsown world. And I don't mean that if its downloaded alot people might be able to get a physical copy but rather if it shows up that there is a strong audience for this sort of thing it might get an official release which was what i figured the point of STV and its predecessor with DND adventure league was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T02:45:23-08:00","id":1180107,"title":"","content":"The point of the community content programs is to monetize fan content. It's always been about that. Fans get to use official trade dress, and publish their work for some money, and the company gets to profit off of doing the work to setup the guidelines and provide some elements to use. The point of them has never been to use fan content as a stepping stone to official books. Martin even said (I can't remember if it was an interview or a con panel... maybe he's said it more than once) before they set up the ST Vault, that if they decide to do an official book because fans make something that catches on, it'll be a different product that's developed by WW, not a promotion of a fan piece to an official one. Though he was clearly talking about things like city books, with the idea that they might do an official city book, but they'd do something to help fan city books for the same city get out to the public.<br /> <br /> I can't entirely blame them on that though. Turning a fan product, even one created under a community content program, into an official product would be a contracting nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:01:28-08:00","id":1180139,"title":"","content":"That's more what I was imagining? That &quot;hey a this Vampire: asskicking edition is selling gold maybe we should make a variant like that too?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:16:12-08:00","id":1180145,"title":"","content":"Ah.... sorry, I was reading that more direct fan to official.<br /> <br /> In general, it could happen, though in specific it seems unlikely. Both because WW set up the ST Vault to limit such products from getting in, and because WW seems to have zero interest in it. Even if WW as going to consider it... big books of optional rules are rarely something you see for at least a few years down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T13:56:17-08:00","id":1182697,"title":"","content":"EDIT: And then I realize I do not actually want to get into this conversation, let alone revive it seven days later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-05-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T17:42:31-08:00","id":1182757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1182697#post1182697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And then I realize I do not actually want to get into this conversation, let alone revive it seven days later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is something I do all the time, here. No worries!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T17:42:45-08:00","id":1182758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1182697#post1182697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And then I realize I do not actually want to get into this conversation, let alone revive it seven days later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I gave myself a good, hard thought and decided I can do lot more productive stuff with my time, than arguing about these things to no end with a small cadre of people I won't agree anyway, on a forum, due to too different baseline views on things. Like, instead I can read books, work out, study, work on other things in my life, watch something, etc. It's literally a waste of hours, would take too much explaining, back-and-forth arguing, digging up things and without any positive outcome. Especially in text. Literally all the arguments were made at this point, over the years on these boards, what could change in opinions, were already been said. So, I called it a day too. Just doesn't worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T17:59:07-08:00","id":1182767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1182758#post1182758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I gave myself a good, hard thought and decided I can do lot more productive stuff with my time, than arguing about these things to no end with a small cadre of people I won't agree anyway, on a forum, due to too different baseline views on things. Like, instead I can read books, work out, study, work on other things in my life, watch something, etc. It's literally a waste of hours, would take too much explaining, back-and-forth arguing, digging up things and without any positive outcome. Especially in text. Literally all the arguments were made at this point, over the years on these boards, what could change in opinions, were already been said. So, I called it a day too. Just doesn't worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly I'd like to see your opinions when we actually have something more substantial. I may not agree with you but I find perspectives I don't agree with on material helps me get a better view on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T18:19:24-08:00","id":1182772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1182767#post1182767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly I'd like to see your opinions <b>when we actually have something more substantial.</b> I may not agree with you but I find perspectives I don't agree with on material helps me get a better view on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis added. I'm totally willing, and will be, to discuss and debate actual information regarding V5, or WW's direction with the new editions. It's just at this point we have too little info and the whole topic is just too loaded for some people and constantly brings up endless political arguments. Don't get me wrong, IRL, I enjoy meaningful political argument, I always learn something from it. I just feel less and less inclination to do it on a forum and in text, by sacrificing hours and hours of my time.<br /> <br /> When we have the game, it'll be good to discuss the handling of certain topics in the setting, the quality of writing, the art direction, the rules, and all the interesting stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T02:51:40-08:00","id":1182848,"title":"","content":"What I've seen of the setting, writing, art direction and rules has been interesting at best and bad most of the time.<br /> LARP should always be second to the tabletop, subjectively, but I think they've almost proved that objectively it should be second if the series started as a tabletop.<br /> <br /> As for politics. I'd love to discuss that, but I've got no inclination to believe that they'll be smart about it. They've combined dark and edgy with safe space mentality and compromise.<br /> World of darkness is great because it appeals to both extreme left and extreme right, with the assumption that society as-is is fucked. Now both left and right can look at different things in WoD and identify it with their viewpoint, even if they have the opposite viewpoint to someone else. It's a bit like how <i>south park </i>can lampoon everything and you'd usually assume it's on your side unless it's attacking you in a particular episode, in which case you can write that one off and maybe enjoy the next episode. If you don't keep that neutrality, it goes to shit. Once you start overtly going X is right, Y is wrong, your criticism becomes total crap. And I know the freelancers at onyx path have been guilty of this, but from NWW I'd expect more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T12:37:47-08:00","id":1183020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1182848#post1182848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I've seen of the setting, writing, art direction and rules has been interesting at best and bad most of the time.<br /> LARP should always be second to the tabletop, subjectively, but I think they've almost proved that objectively it should be second if the series started as a tabletop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quoting this but it sort of an open question: what about the current rules in the Alpha slice says to you that these are &quot;larp inspired&quot; ? I personally found as someone who does both that they came off with the sort of complexity and finicky nature one gets from a heavy Table top game and not the sort of thing you'd want to be running at a larp with a much higher percentage of Players to Sts. I mean I currently find the hunger mechanics annoying but that's just seeing it at a 3-5 player game. I can't imagine a game with 10 to 20 people or a large event with 50 to 100 and it not just becoming a complete and utter clusterfuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T02:43:27-08:00","id":1184308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1182772#post1182772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis added. I'm totally willing, and will be, to discuss and debate actual information regarding V5, or WW's direction with the new editions. It's just at this point we have too little info and the whole topic is just too loaded for some people and constantly brings up endless political arguments. Don't get me wrong, IRL, I enjoy meaningful political argument, I always learn something from it. I just feel less and less inclination to do it on a forum and in text, by sacrificing hours and hours of my time.<br /> <br /> When we have the game, it'll be good to discuss the handling of certain topics in the setting, the quality of writing, the art direction, the rules, and all the interesting stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>While partially true, it is worth noting that some of the point of playtests and early releasing of material is to get people talking, to weed out bad concepts, to establish direction, and the like. <br /> <br /> While it is true that we do not have a great deal of info, only speaking for myself and some of the things I have heard, there is a great deal I find troubling, and I imagine that a lot of folks with similar concerns are aiming to try to get those things fixed, looked at, or discussed <i>before</i> they become worse.<br /> <br /> I am also a bit concerned that the new WW seems very unwilling to give much definitive or meaningful discourse on plans, efforts, findings, or whatever. We hear, or had been hearing a bit earlier on all of these grand plans, (very little specifics), but it feels more like wishful thinking than feasable, especially considering just how little seems to have come from it all after some months.<br /> <br /> For instance, there have been two, fairly contentious &quot;video games&quot;, (do they really even count as video games???), and a dice roller app for all the talk of crossmedia building up the franchise. Heard a rumor of a WtA computer game the other day, (note I said rumor), but given the history of WoD video games, Ill believe it when I see it, and even then, not sure I really care, too much. But, for the WtA fans, I'd be happy if it works out well.<br /> <br /> As for the plans for V5, (not to mention W5, M5, W5, etc...?), from everything I have heard about the propossed setting, I, again only speaking for myself, but know I am not alone, am not finding it either interesting or desirable, and honestly hope they do a complete 180\u00b0 turn, on just about everything hinted or propossed.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, that leaves me, as a long time VtM fan and collector, not in a position of wait and see, but unsure if I even want to consider bothering after it comes out at all. Not a great place for fan's mind sets, and while I am unsure just how common this is, across the board, I do know it is something I have heard from others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T09:24:29-08:00","id":1184427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184308#post1184308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heard a rumor of a WtA computer game the other day, (note I said rumor), but given the history of WoD video games, Ill believe it when I see it, and even then, not sure I really care, too much. But, for the WtA fans, I'd be happy if it works out well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than a rumor. <br /> <br /> They've done a number of interviews and have shown concept art for the last few months.<br /> <br /> I mean, Paradox has only had the license for a little over a year.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Give them some times, folks.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> There'll be some hits, and there will be some misses. Same as any company.<br /> <br /> *runs to read more Wraith 20<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T10:59:06-08:00","id":1184452,"title":"","content":"As oppossed to the last one or two?<br /> <br /> \ud83d\ude1b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T13:41:59-08:00","id":1184507,"title":"","content":"The current WtA game is certainly in progress. There's a difference between a project that gets cancelled like the WoD MMO, and things that are just rumors (Half-Life 3 for example, let alone Half-Life 2, Episode 3).<br /> <br /> That said, Paradox bought the IPs over two years ago, and part of their deal with CCP was all the WoD MMO stuff (so Paradox owns a bunch of video game assets for the WoD that they didn't have to produce themselves), and their three product releases so far haven't exactly been... well... hits. And their lack of hits isn't just the controversies with creators.<br /> <br /> Sure, two years isn't exactly much time. Though they've also overpromised in terms of what they thought they could get done in that time. They want to be on Netflix in two years, and V5 isn't even close to out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T15:40:37-08:00","id":1184538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184308#post1184308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am also a bit concerned that the new WW seems very unwilling to give much definitive or meaningful discourse on plans, efforts, findings, or whatever. We hear, or had been hearing a bit earlier on all of these grand plans, (very little specifics), but it feels more like wishful thinking than feasable, especially considering just how little seems to have come from it all after some months.</div> </div> </div> </div>STs Guild launched, multiple lines got added to it. Community site is under betatesting (I think). People are talking about the news, even outside the WoD community. I'd say, they are certainly doind things, not to mention the LARP side. I wouldn't expect much more before V5's debut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For instance, there have been two, fairly contentious &quot;video games&quot;, (do they really even count as video games???), and a dice roller app for all the talk of crossmedia building up the franchise. Heard a rumor of a WtA computer game the other day, (note I said rumor), but given the history of WoD video games, Ill believe it when I see it, and even then, not sure I really care, too much. But, for the WtA fans, I'd be happy if it works out well. </div> </div> </div>As the others said, it seems to be happening, not just talk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the plans for V5, (not to mention W5, M5, W5, etc...?), from everything I have heard about the propossed setting, I, again only speaking for myself, but know I am not alone, am not finding it either interesting or desirable, and honestly hope they do a complete 180\u00b0 turn, on just about everything hinted or propossed.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, that leaves me, as a long time VtM fan and collector, not in a position of wait and see, but unsure if I even want to consider bothering after it comes out at all. Not a great place for fan's mind sets, and while I am unsure just how common this is, across the board, I do know it is something I have heard from others. </div> </div> </div>I totally understand that and I'm pretty sure there will be heated arguments about the setting changes after the book(s) came out. I'm currently ambigous about it and, for me, it's precisely wait and see at this point. I've seen and heard a lot of things I liked, but some of the other stuff felt way too out of what I consider Masquerade or even felt unnecessarily Requiem-y, like the forced isolation between cities * for example . However, even my final view on those elements will depend on execution and frankly, the profoundness of the changes. I see the potential in what they've shared, but I see the possibility that I'll put down the book and say &quot;well, fine and dandy, but it isn't Masquerade&quot; at the end. I don't want the setting to be frozen in time, but taking it too far from the original is sure a looming possibility too, based on what we've seen and heard so far. That includes setting, rules, art direction (which, for me, will be a huge thing). Of course, it is a highly personal judgment. What could be cool to me and an interesting new direction might be too much for you. And I'm absolutely not sure that it won't be too much for me either. It's just, at this point, I see the possibility for this to be good too and unlike some others, I'm not harboring any hard feelings toward them. For me, at this point it could turn out either way. Again, for you, it could be already too far and that's okay too.<br /> <br /> *Or the stabs on gothic-punk and urban fantasy, yeah those lifted my eyebrows considerably... still, I'm not sure what Martin really meant when he said that and the last interview with him and Tobias on the Darker Days radio podcast well, they've said a lot of things I could only nod at. They've also elaborated on things in a way I've found appealing. So yeah, I decided I'd remain open-minded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-10-2018, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T16:54:38-08:00","id":1184556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184538#post1184538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">STs Guild launched, multiple lines got added to it. Community site is under betatesting (I think).</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST Vault getting launched isn't really that big of a deal. It's some work, yes, but OBS's community content does that vast majority of that for them. &quot;Multiple lines,&quot; is a bit of a questionable claim. You can only do VtM, all that's been &quot;added&quot; is Dark Ages, Victorian, and Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom. Everything has to be VtM rules, so you can't have werewolves that are compatible with WtA, only lupines using VtM rules. You can't even use Kindred of the East yet. It seems like they'll eventually get the whole thing in there, but there doesn't seem to be a reason to be going as slow as they are.<br /> <br /> The Community site is in betatest... though it's not entirely clear what that means. But I'm not even sure what they want a community page to be? There's a basic, &quot;put your troupe/store/etc.&quot; on Google Maps thing. There's a mess of information and art that's not clear what it's for exactly. You can put characters up there. There's a store. &quot;community site&quot; seems lacking in, well, community tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T17:15:40-08:00","id":1184561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184556#post1184556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ST Vault getting launched isn't really that big of a deal. It's some work, yes, but OBS's community content does that vast majority of that for them. &quot;Multiple lines,&quot; is a bit of a questionable claim. You can only do VtM, all that's been &quot;added&quot; is Dark Ages, Victorian, and Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom. Everything has to be VtM rules, so you can't have werewolves that are compatible with WtA, only lupines using VtM rules. You can't even use Kindred of the East yet. It seems like they'll eventually get the whole thing in there, but there doesn't seem to be a reason to be going as slow as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from being a side-project? Still they put up guidelines, art packs, so that is work to do. I'm contended with the tempo, they're adding things on a steady stream. WotC Only has FR and Ravenloft, I think on DM's guild without any such helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Community site is in betatest... though it's not entirely clear what that means. But I'm not even sure what they want a community page to be? There's a basic, &quot;put your troupe/store/etc.&quot; on Google Maps thing. There's a mess of information and art that's not clear what it's for exactly. You can put characters up there. There's a store. &quot;community site&quot; seems lacking in, well, community tools. </div> </div> </div>Because it's not finished yet? It's a mess, right now, yes, but it's under development. I think it'll be a good thing, when finalized, tabletop material, maybe chat rooms/messageboards addod, news and updates periodically uploaded, events shared, metaplot happenings followed, etc.<br /> <br /> I think I see what's their intention with it, it just takes time. I won't be suprised if they'd announce the launch of the finalized site along V5, or shortly before/after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T01:52:35-08:00","id":1184664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184561#post1184561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from being a side-project?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the only thin they're visibly doing with regular positive progress... I'm not sure that's such a thing to leave on the side. V5 is in progress, but we get very infrequent updates on that. The WtA video game isn't actually being done by WW. What the heck are the staff at WW that aren't part of the V5 development team... doing besides this exactly?<br /> <br /> It's also not like we're talking a lot of difficult work. The guidelines updates so far have only been to include that people can include someone that they couldn't before. The aren't producing new art of the art packs as far as I can tell, and the layout/trade dress stuff rather than page and cover art is already collected. Like I said, yeah, it's work. But ~2 months to get Victorian Vampire or Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom done? It's not that much work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....I think on DM's guild without any such helps. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it's not finished yet? It's a mess, right now, yes, but it's under development. </div> </div> </div>It's a beta test. Beta tests shouldn't be this much of a mess. Beta means all the primary functions are ready and the product needs to be refined and polished. If they're going to include chat rooms, or forums, or a news section... those should be there now even if not 100% ready. I shouldn't have to guess if they're going to include those features or not by now if they're beta testing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T02:06:11-08:00","id":1184667,"title":"","content":"I'm rather surprised we never saw more than the hunger mechanics, I mean if they want to have the book out this year.. they probably need to have the manuscript done fairly soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T06:18:50-08:00","id":1184710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184507#post1184507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">heir three product releases so far haven't exactly been... well... hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Hits? Maybe not. But they didn't need to be.<br /> <br /> Do you have a link to the sales figures and cost of development for the two interactive(and pretty crappy) story games they released on Steam?<br /> <br /> I know they made WW money. And in the end, they were happy with the sales results--especially in terms of what it cost them to produce them. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 02-11-2018, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T06:21:17-08:00","id":1184711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184452#post1184452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As oppossed to the last one or two?<br /> <br /> \ud83d\ude1b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. I think we should always judge a new company's work with an IP on previous companies uses of the IP.<br /> <br /> That is totally 100% fair.<br /> <br /> ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T09:09:17-08:00","id":1184759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184711#post1184711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I think we should always judge a new company's work with an IP on previous companies uses of the IP.<br /> That is totally 100% fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say. One could also say it is perfectly fair to look at it as a property, rather than who specifically owns it, and if the new WW is wanting to reclaim White Wolfness, doesn't that include the history of, at least Heart of Gaia, if not also WoD Online? <br /> <br /> Im not trying to sling s#!% at the new WW, just pointing out my original point was that there have already been many promises made, many hopes raised, and multiple attempts at cross media. How/Why, exactly, is this one any different? Anything tangable, or just more &quot;we have big plans. Big plans and stuff. Wait and see&quot;.<br /> <br /> If anything, I am complaining about their production strategy. Have something notable before you start making all these promises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 02-11-2018, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T09:14:21-08:00","id":1184762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184759#post1184759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard to say. One could also say it is perfectly fair to look at it as a property, rather than who specifically owns it, and if the new WW is wanting to reclaim White Wolfness, doesn't that include the history of, at least Heart of Gaia, if not also WoD Online?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> lol. Sure.<br /> <br /> But that also includes, arguably, one of the greatest computer rpgs of all time(Bloodlines), another damn fine one(Redemption), andTHREE very popular Hunter the Reckoning games.<br /> <br /> So, you can spin it however you'd like. I'm just saying I think Paradox and Cyanide deserve a bit more leeway with their new Werewolf game.<br /> <br /> If you disagree, that's fine too. Don't buy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T09:22:01-08:00","id":1184767,"title":"","content":"You caught me in the middle of editing. Sorry, deployed and using a cell phone that is not very compatable with these forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T10:31:24-08:00","id":1184787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184710#post1184710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. Hits? Maybe not. But they didn't need to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably would have been better if they were though... right? A combined ~60% positive reviews on Steam for both isn't really a great execution of their first venture out into the wider world beyond the WoD fandom (and a good number of the positive reviews basically say that it's only positive for WoD fans and people just there for the IF should skip it). Both of the curator reviews are negative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have a link to the sales figures and cost of development for the two interactive(and pretty crappy) story games they released on Steam? </div> </div> </div>Why does the money side of it matter? Is that all we, as fans, care about? That it makes WW a profit? I don't want RPGs from a company who's first principle is, &quot;what makes us the most money,&quot; because it means quality is one of the first things that'll be dropped. One thing Steam does let you see, is a graph of reviews. These things had a huge number of reviews when they game out (positive and negative). The community page for them have been dead for a year. Basically their sales were all based on people buying blind because it was relatively cheap and the WoD brand has some value. The VtM and HtR video games still have people talking about them.<br /> <br /> Burning that perceived value with two &quot;pretty crappy&quot; products does what? Get a bunch of people to be more apprehensive about future games? Even the old &quot;negative attention is still attention&quot; thing doesn't justify it to a larger strategy because nobody actually cares about them. Any change to capitalize on a moment of controversy is long past with no future product to get attention towards.<br /> <br /> If they made some money of it? OK. Whatever. They have Paradox's money, they don't need to pump out small products to turn a profit just to exist. Paradox seems happy to bankroll them during their first few years largely dedicated to development; and there's no way the Preludes are paying for the money WW is currently spending.<br /> <br /> If they didn't need to be hits... what did they need to be? Why does it matter?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T11:59:03-08:00","id":1184832,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the only folks I personally know that loved Bloodlines either had already been fans, or it was their introduction into TT RPGs WoD. Non-(TT RPG) gamers, again that I personally know, had, ... mixed reviews, much favoring against it.<br /> <br /> Hell, I couldn't get a single person to try Redemption, which I loved.<br /> <br /> While Im not a fan of the sort of &quot;game&quot; the most recent two are, the sheer amount of wankery was off putting enough for me to not even bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 02-12-2018, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T16:37:48-08:00","id":1184946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1184832#post1184832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the only folks I personally know that loved Bloodlines either had already been fans, or it was their introduction into TT RPGs WoD. Non-(TT RPG) gamers, again that I personally know, had, ... mixed reviews, much favoring against it.<br /> <br /> Hell, I couldn't get a single person to try Redemption, which I loved.<br /> <br /> While Im not a fan of the sort of &quot;game&quot; the most recent two are, the sheer amount ou SJW wankery was off putting enough for me to not even bother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your referencing anecdotal evidence. Which...is fine. But Bloodlines is still widely regarding as an amazing RPG with technical problems. Six more months, and we may be putting it into some top 10 lists of all time(and some publications already DO).<br /> <br /> Bloodlines IS my favorite video game of all time. Redemption, not far behind it. The Hunter the Reckoning games were all great fun, too.<br /> <br /> And while they were my introduction into TT games(which is not a bad thing), I am a gamer first. And as someone who loves video games, I sure as fuck loved all the World of Darkness video games(save for the two interactive stories which I don't count as &quot;games&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And while I do agree with you on your last point, this is certainly not the forum to state that in; and if I were you, I'd delete it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T03:59:45-08:00","id":1185083,"title":"","content":"I think you misunderstand my point. I loved both Bloodlines and Redemption. I think I like Redemption more, honestly. I also loved the HtR games. However, and yes this is anecdotal, in my experience they did very little to bring in new fans. That is not to say it didn't happen at all, only from what I have seen, and heard from others, and I believe this was even brought up with the early nWW youtube videos, it mostly attracted existing fans.<br /> <br /> The HtR games are a little different, in that they largely came out with the TT game, and played very much like a genre game, (in the sense they could have been called anything and had a few names scrubbed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T12:01:04-08:00","id":1191409,"title":"","content":"There's another big game that'll end up coming out this year that might pose a threat to 2018 being the year of Vampire V: the 30th anniversary edition of West End Star Wars. You know, the d6 game. You know, the best Star Wars RPG. Okay, technically it's more of a reprint than anything, but Star Wars d6 is a big name.<br /> <br /> It also relies on whether Wrath &amp; Glory comes out this year. But given that it's supposed to replace a well-liked line of games and it throws the focus of said games out the window I don't think it's going to be much competition for Vampire V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T21:46:38-08:00","id":1191532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191409#post1191409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another big game that'll end up coming out this year that might pose a threat to 2018 being the year of Vampire V: the 30th anniversary edition of West End Star Wars. You know, the d6 game. You know, the best Star Wars RPG. Okay, technically it's more of a reprint than anything, but Star Wars d6 is a big name.<br /> <br /> It also relies on whether Wrath &amp; Glory comes out this year. But given that it's supposed to replace a well-liked line of games and it throws the focus of said games out the window I don't think it's going to be much competition for Vampire V.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A reprint of Star Wars d6 is barely on the radar... especially in light of the fact that FFG still has the rights to Starwars. Now if someone were making a Newish edition D6 SW maybe. As for Wrath and Glory, it lets you play just about everything right from the box as intended.. while v5 won't even have sabbat or independent options off the bat. Seems like any issues Wrath and Glory might have v5 would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T22:25:10-08:00","id":1191541,"title":"","content":"While it never pulls in big numbers, and I don't expect it to because it's an older game. Bloodlines is well received in twitch and regularly seems to get praised when it gets brought up. I am personally just fine waiting until the actual Werewolf game is out and judging it on it's own merits rather than making preconceived notions of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T04:43:07-08:00","id":1191592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191532#post1191532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reprint of Star Wars d6 is barely on the radar... especially in light of the fact that FFG still has the rights to Starwars. Now if someone were making a Newish edition D6 SW maybe. As for Wrath and Glory, it lets you play just about everything right from the box as intended.. while v5 won't even have sabbat or independent options off the bat. Seems like any issues Wrath and Glory might have v5 would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that FFG is the one releasing the Star Wars d6 game that's not going to be an issue.<br /> <br /> And Wrath &amp; Glory's problem is exactly that: it lets you play <i>everything</i> out of the box. There's no focus, no identity the game sets out to be. It's not like a Vampire book where you can play Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarch or independent out of the box: it's like if Vampire, Changeling, Hunter, Mage and Demon were all put into a single game and you were told to make your own game out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T05:34:09-08:00","id":1191599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191541#post1191541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it never pulls in big numbers, and I don't expect it to because it's an older game. Bloodlines is well received in twitch and regularly seems to get praised when it gets brought up. I am personally just fine waiting until the actual Werewolf game is out and judging it on it's own merits rather than making preconceived notions of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not on topic, but if Bloodlines were released today(with a graphics nudge and fewer bugs) across all platforms, it would've sold much, MUCH better and had a giant presence on most gaming social media platforms.<br /> <br /> People are still screaming for a Bloodlines-like game on Facebook and Twitter almost 15 years later.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:10:01-08:00","id":1191629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191592#post1191592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that FFG is the one releasing the Star Wars d6 game that's not going to be an issue.<br /> <br /> And Wrath &amp; Glory's problem is exactly that: it lets you play <i>everything</i> out of the box. There's no focus, no identity the game sets out to be. It's not like a Vampire book where you can play Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarch or independent out of the box: it's like if Vampire, Changeling, Hunter, Mage and Demon were all put into a single game and you were told to make your own game out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I loved <i>Only War</i>, <i>Rogue Trader</i> and <i>Black Crusade</i> and liked <i>Dark Heresy</i> for that very reason, that each was their own thing, focused on their own types of games. While Wrath &amp; Glory appears to be going for a scattershot, all-in-one approach that I'm not happy about. Even if it's just the Imperium, that's a <i>lot</i> of wildly different groups and types of games. Just look at the previous run of 40K RPGs. There are four just on groups within the Imperium, each of which are thematically different and can play quite differently.<br /> <br /> As for V5 and only having the Camarilla 7 as playable, that's not really anything new. Remember, 1E VtM (and I think the 2E too) only had the Camarilla 7 as playable and no real sect options. It took time before the Anarchs, Sabbat, Independents and Bloodlines were fleshed out and added. And frankly, the Sabbat and some of the Independent Clans aren't really playable without their respective books. Yeah, you could play them with VtM Rev or V20 but it's hard to get into those groups with just the Core books.<br /> <br /> So just having the Camarilla 7 in the V5 Core book isn't really a big deal to me because if I'm going to run a V5 game (or any VtM game) with new players, I'm going to have them playing Camarilla with the Seven Clans because of the ease of access they present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:22:36-08:00","id":1191656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191629#post1191629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. I loved <i>Only War</i>, <i>Rogue Trader</i> and <i>Black Crusade</i> and liked <i>Dark Heresy</i> for that very reason, that each was their own thing, focused on their own types of games. While Wrath &amp; Glory appears to be going for a scattershot, all-in-one approach that I'm not happy about. Even if it's just the Imperium, that's a <i>lot</i> of wildly different groups and types of games. Just look at the previous run of 40K RPGs. There are four just on groups within the Imperium, each of which are thematically different and can play quite differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets even worse when you find out that the game has four core &quot;races&quot;: Human, Space Marine, Eldar and Ork. Humans and Space Marines can on paper work together, but unless you play a really out there game of Rogue Trader or a radical Inquisitor you're not going to pull that off in a normal game. It's like trying to make a troupe of a Brujah, Red Talon, Wayward Hunter and Nephandus and get them to play nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T17:07:50-08:00","id":1191777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191629#post1191629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for V5 and only having the Camarilla 7 as playable, that's not really anything new. Remember, 1E VtM (and I think the 2E too) only had the Camarilla 7 as playable and no real sect options. It took time before the Anarchs, Sabbat, Independents and Bloodlines were fleshed out and added. And frankly, the Sabbat and some of the Independent Clans aren't really playable without their respective books. Yeah, you could play them with VtM Rev or V20 but it's hard to get into those groups with just the Core books.<br /> <br /> So just having the Camarilla 7 in the V5 Core book isn't really a big deal to me because if I'm going to run a V5 game (or any VtM game) with new players, I'm going to have them playing Camarilla with the Seven Clans because of the ease of access they present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. I've had some chagrin about not including the Sabbat and the Independents from the get-go, because, well, I started with Revised and thus, the game feels incomplete that way. However, since that, I thought about it a lot and I think it is actually not a bad idea. Having the core 7 clans and a Cam and Anarch setting book as the starting point allows for an easy entry point for new gamers and considerably refocusing of themes and mood, thus, reassuring the game's identity.<br /> <br /> However, I'm really hoping the rest will come quickly after, because well, the game <i>would be </i>incomplete without them and I can't really picture a metplot working that way, or more accurately, working without having the setting totally rewritten and I don1t think they'll go that far. Remember, the Sabbat's crusade is a big deal (and i'm starting to get what they want with it, from Beckett's) and even the Alpha playtest's epilogue Chicago scene had a Settite representing the Tremere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T00:15:03-08:00","id":1191858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191656#post1191656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gets even worse when you find out that the game has four core &quot;races&quot;: Human, Space Marine, Eldar and Ork. Humans and Space Marines can on paper work together, but unless you play a really out there game of Rogue Trader or a radical Inquisitor you're not going to pull that off in a normal game. It's like trying to make a troupe of a Brujah, Red Talon, Wayward Hunter and Nephandus and get them to play nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rogue Trader with his retinue.. wow that was SO hard. Both Eldar and Orks have mercenary offshoots. This is before we take into account the 8th edition timeline changes. But ignoring that both v20 and revised had full splat writeups for Cam, sabbat without the intent that say you'd be playing a Tzim, a Tremere, a Salubri all in the same group, having all your options in the same book doesn't mean all options are intended to be played.<br /> <br /> Finally I will repeat again, v5 is at least as radically different from what came before as Wrath and Glory is for the various FFG itterations of 40k, saying that one of them is going to be vastly panned by fans while one is clearly going to be anticipated is dubious at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T04:25:54-08:00","id":1191886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1168631-v5-is-the-most-anticipated-rpg-of-2018-second-try?p=1191599#post1191599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not on topic, but if Bloodlines were released today(with a graphics nudge and fewer bugs) across all platforms, it would've sold much, MUCH better and had a giant presence on most gaming social media platforms.<br /> <br /> People are still screaming for a Bloodlines-like game on Facebook and Twitter almost 15 years later.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am curious if this would be true. The market has changed a lot since Bloodlines came out, and things that were innovative, new, or uncommon for video game rpgs are pretty standard now, (multiple routes to accomplish tasks, good/evil/neutal playstyles or endings, heavier focus on story, etc...).<br /> <br /> Additionally, VtM/WoD was going very strong when Bloodlines came out, but is less so, now. And the nastolgia factor, (for instance the recent Star Wars movies), can be hit or miss. There is also the possibility that some of the things in Bloodlines that made the game what it is might not have been allowed to fly these days.<br /> <br /> I would like to think Bloodlines would, as it is a great game, and one I still play, but I could honestly see it going either way.<br /> <br /> I'd, however wish that there were more games, particularly VtM or WoD similar to Bloodlines, (and Redemption).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T10:37:54-08:00","id":1191991,"title":"","content":"I think more than nostalgia, what's hit or miss for something like Bloodlines being made today is customer tolerance for games that need a lot of patching.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons Bloodlines has the legs it does (esp. compared to the other WoD video games) is a strong fan mod community that helped significantly extended the fun of the game by doing things like restoring dropped quests, fixing bugs, and adding general game play improvements.<br /> <br /> There are certainly franchises where that's considered part of the way you play (Elder Scrolls), but in general people expect games to not need fan mods to actually feel done. If you want to court the fan mod community, you need to make a good game and accessible mod tools. Why should someone play a game that needs serious patching, and the company isn't doing it, when they can play an equal quality game that's actually done, and has decent tools and a fan community that's adding to the game with new missions/etc. instead of fixing it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T16:23:19-08:00","id":1192084,"title":"","content":"I played Bloodlines without any mods and I enjoyed it. Just didn't bother with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T02:10:45-08:00","id":1192179,"title":"","content":"I have as well, (minus the original mod needed to actually complete the game), and I agree, it is pretty good.<br /> <br /> I view that angle as more extenuating circumatances though, not really the fault of the game itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}